Object.assign(EVENT_NARRATIVE_TRANSLATIONS.es, {
    "The Abandoned Camp": "El campamento abandonado",
    "A camp in a side chamber, left in a hurry. The fire is cold. The tent still stands, one pole leaning.\n\nBedrolls, a cooking pot, a bag half unpacked. Nobody came back for any of it.": "Un campamento en una cámara lateral, abandonado a toda prisa. El fuego está frío. La tienda sigue en pie, con un poste inclinado.\n\nPetates, una olla, una bolsa a medio vaciar. Nadie volvió a por nada.",
    "Sleep in the tent": "Dormir en la tienda",
    "In the night, something walks around the tent. Then it stops walking.": "De noche, algo camina alrededor de la tienda. Luego deja de caminar.",
    "You sleep. Nobody comes.\n\nIn the morning the camp is exactly as they left it.": "Duermes. No viene nadie.\n\nPor la mañana, el campamento está tal como lo dejaron.",
    "Look around the camp": "Explorar el campamento",
    "Behind the tent, half under the bedrolls, you find one of them.\n\nHis sword is out of its sheath. The blade is clean. There is not a mark on him.\n\nHe did not die fighting. His face looks as if he saw a ghost.": "Detrás de la tienda, medio tapado por los petates, encuentras a uno de ellos.\n\nSu espada está fuera de la vaina. La hoja está limpia. No tiene ni un rasguño.\n\nNo murió luchando. Tiene cara de haber visto un fantasma.",
    "Take his backpack": "Coger su mochila",
    "You are still crouched over him when the tent flap moves behind you.\n\nThere is no wind down here.": "Sigues agachado sobre él cuando la entrada de la tienda se mueve a tu espalda.\n\nAquí abajo no hay viento.",
    "Nothing moves. You leave him the rest.": "Nada se mueve. Le dejas lo demás.",
    "Take his sword": "Coger su espada",
    "Take his armor": "Coger su armadura",
    "Bury him and pray": "Enterrarlo y rezar",
    "You leave his things where they are. The ground is soft enough.\n\nWhen you finish the prayer, the chamber is very quiet. You stand up lighter than you knelt down.": "Dejas sus cosas donde están. La tierra está bastante blanda.\n\nCuando terminas de rezar, la cámara está en silencio. Te levantas con menos peso del que sentías al arrodillarte.",
    "Leave him": "Dejarlo",
    "You leave him as you found him. You do not look at his face again.": "Lo dejas como lo encontraste. No vuelves a mirarle la cara.",
    "Leave the camp": "Salir del campamento",
    "You leave the camp as it is. Whoever left it is not coming back.": "Dejas el campamento como está. Quien lo abandonó no va a volver.",
    "A small black music box lies under the rubble — lid cracked, one brass leg twitching.\n\nAs you lean in, it plays three notes and snaps shut.": "Bajo los escombros hay una cajita de música negra: tapa agrietada, una pata de latón que se mueve.\n\nCuando te acercas, toca tres notas y se cierra de golpe.",
    "Force it open": "Abrirla a la fuerza",
    "You pry at the lid.": "Haces palanca en la tapa.",
    "Open it carefully": "Abrirla con cuidado",
    "The lock gives. Inside, where the cylinder should turn, a cog is missing.\n\nThe box looks at you — somehow — then grows two more legs and falls in behind you.": "La cerradura cede. Dentro, donde debería girar el cilindro, falta un engranaje.\n\nLa caja te mira, de algún modo. Luego le salen dos patas más y empieza a seguirte.",
    "Leave it alone": "Dejarla en paz",
    "You step over it and keep walking.\n\nTen steps later: small metal feet on the stones behind you.": "Pasas por encima y sigues andando.\n\nDiez pasos después: patitas de metal sobre las piedras, detrás de ti.",
    "A goblin steps out from behind a broken machine, sniffs the air, and coughs.\n\n": "Un goblin sale de detrás de una máquina rota, olfatea el aire y tose.\n\n",
    "\"Snatch Box. Charge went first. I can smell the powder from here. Nothing left to seat a cog in.\"\n\n": "«Caja Ratera. La carga estalló antes. Huelo la pólvora desde aquí. Ya no queda dónde encajar un engranaje».\n\n",
    "He looks at your boots as if a box might still be hiding there. It is not.": "Te mira las botas, como si la caja aún pudiera esconderse ahí. No está.",
    "A goblin steps out from behind a broken machine and points at the music box.\n\n\"Sleepy Snatch Box. Old robber model. Plays a song, puffs smoke, hero sleeps, pockets empty. Very illegal. Very profitable.\"\n\nThe box hides behind your boot.": "Un goblin sale de detrás de una máquina rota y señala la caja de música.\n\n«Caja Ratera Somnífera. Viejo modelo de ladrones. Toca una canción, suelta humo, héroe duerme, bolsillos vacíos. Muy ilegal. Muy rentable».\n\nLa caja se esconde detrás de tu bota.",
    "\"You found its heart cog. Give it here — I can seat it properly. Or improperly. Depends on payment.\"": "«Encontraste su engranaje central. Dámelo, puedo encajarlo bien. O mal. Depende del pago».",
    "\"No cog? I have spares. Spare parts cost extra.\"": "«¿Sin engranaje? Tengo repuestos. Las piezas se cobran aparte».",
    "Refuse to pay": "Negarte a pagar",
    "Give him an unwanted card for spare parts": "Darle una carta para piezas",
    "Pay 30 coins for full repair": "Repararla por 30 monedas",
    "He shrugs. \"Ash is ash. I don't do funerals.\"\n\nHe is already back behind the machine before you turn away.": "Se encoge de hombros. «Ceniza es ceniza. No hago funerales».\n\nYa está detrás de la máquina cuando te das la vuelta.",
    "The Mirror Twin": "El doble del espejo",
    "A dry corner. You sit down and shut your eyes.\n\nWhen you open them, someone is sitting across from you. Hooded, cross-legged, wearing your face. The scar on your chin is on his other side.\n\nYou scratch your nose. He scratches his nose. His knees touch yours.": "Un rincón seco. Te sientas y cierras los ojos.\n\nCuando los abres, hay alguien sentado frente a ti. Con capucha, piernas cruzadas y tu cara. La cicatriz de tu barbilla está en el otro lado de la suya.\n\nTe rascas la nariz. Él se rasca la nariz. Sus rodillas tocan las tuyas.",
    "Give him a shard": "Darle un fragmento",
    "He holds the shard up. A face looks back from it, not yours. He turns to look closer.": "Levanta el fragmento. En él se refleja una cara, pero no la tuya. Se vuelve para mirar mejor.",
    "Sneak away": "Escabullirte",
    "You lift your pack one strap at a time and back out of the corner. He doesn't look up.\n\nOn the sixth step the floor stops.\n\nYou land on old rugs beside a dead camp. A note under a stone: \"Day 4. Mirror man STILL here. Going to try sneaking. Don't look back.\"\n\nUnder it, an amulet. You take it and climb out the far side. You don't look back.": "Levantas la mochila, una correa cada vez, y sales del rincón retrocediendo. Él no levanta la vista.\n\nAl sexto paso se acaba el suelo.\n\nAterrizas sobre alfombras viejas junto a un campamento muerto. Una nota bajo una piedra: «Día 4. El hombre del espejo SIGUE aquí. Voy a intentar escabullirme. No mirar atrás».\n\nDebajo hay un amuleto. Lo coges y trepas por el otro lado. No miras atrás.",
    "Give him the Gemseeker's Lens": "Dar la Lente del buscagemas",
    "Even better: his own face, enormous. He presses his nose to it and forgets you.": "Aún mejor: su propia cara, enorme. Pega la nariz y se olvida de ti.",
    "Give him the Hand Mirror": "Darle el Espejo de mano",
    "He looks into the mirror. Another him looks back. He leans in. So does the other one.\n\nWhoosh.\n\nYou pick up the mirror. Your reflection isn't in it. He is, pressed flat against the glass, looking pleased.": "Se mira en el espejo. Otro él le devuelve la mirada. Se acerca. El otro también.\n\nFiu.\n\nRecoges el espejo. Tu reflejo no está. Está él, aplastado contra el cristal, con cara de satisfacción.",
    "Try to out-stare him": "Ganarle sin parpadear",
    "You blink first. He does a small victory dance and wanders off, still dancing. You do not get your rest.": "Parpadeas primero. Hace un bailecito de victoria y se marcha sin dejar de bailar. Te quedas sin descanso.",
    "A shadow crosses the nest. Then again, lower.": "Una sombra pasa sobre el nido. Luego otra vez, más baja.",
    "A nest sits wedged between two fallen pillars — speckled eggs, bent keys, old buttons, and one small brass cog.\n\n": "Un nido encajado entre dos columnas caídas: huevos moteados, llaves dobladas, botones viejos y un pequeño engranaje de latón.\n\n",
    "Search the nest": "Registrar el nido",
    "You reach into the nest.": "Metes la mano en el nido.",
    "The Old Chute": "El viejo conducto",
    "A flagstone tips under your boot. You drop into an old trap chute and slide a long way down in the dark.\n\nWhatever was meant to be waiting at the bottom rotted away years ago. You land unhurt, on something that goes crack.\n\nUnder you is a spider the size of a dog, made of clear crystal. Most of it is in pieces now.": "Una losa se inclina bajo tu bota. Caes en el conducto de una vieja trampa y te deslizas un buen trecho a oscuras.\n\nLo que debía esperarte abajo se pudrió hace años. Aterrizas sin hacerte daño, sobre algo que cruje.\n\nDebajo hay una araña del tamaño de un perro, hecha de cristal transparente. Ahora casi toda está en pedazos.",
    "Take a crystal leg": "Coger una pata de cristal",
    "One leg came off clean. It is cold, and it still catches the light.\n\nAhead of you, in the corner of the pit, is her nest: a heap of crystal eggs, each the size of a fist.": "Una pata se ha desprendido entera. Está fría y aún refleja la luz.\n\nDelante, en un rincón del foso, está su nido: un montón de huevos de cristal, cada uno del tamaño de un puño.",
    "Burn the eggs": "Quemar los huevos",
    "The fireball fills the pit. The eggs pop one by one.\n\nWhen the smoke clears, the heat has fused what is left into a single lump of crystal.": "La bola de fuego llena el foso. Los huevos estallan uno a uno.\n\nCuando se disipa el humo, el calor ha fundido los restos en un solo bloque de cristal.",
    "Smash the eggs": "Romper los huevos",
    "The third egg is already open. So is the fourth.\n\nSmall crystal legs come out of the heap.": "El tercer huevo ya está abierto. El cuarto también.\n\nDel montón salen pequeñas patas de cristal.",
    "You crush them all. It is loud, and nothing answers.\n\nThe shards are worth something.": "Los aplastas todos. Haces mucho ruido. Nada responde.\n\nLos fragmentos valen algo.",
    "Take one egg": "Coger un huevo",
    "You pick the smallest one. It is cold, and heavier than it looks.\n\nSomething inside taps back.": "Eliges el más pequeño. Está frío y pesa más de lo que parece.\n\nAlgo dentro responde con unos golpecitos.",
    "Leave the nest": "Dejar el nido",
    "You leave the eggs where they are and climb out the long way.\n\nHalfway up, below you, one of them cracks.": "Dejas los huevos donde están y trepas por el camino largo.\n\nA mitad de la subida, debajo de ti, uno se resquebraja.",
    "Leave her be": "Dejarla en paz",
    "You climb off her and leave her where she lies.\n\nAhead of you, in the corner of the pit, is her nest: a heap of crystal eggs, each the size of a fist.": "Te apartas de ella y la dejas donde está.\n\nDelante, en un rincón del foso, está su nido: un montón de huevos de cristal, cada uno del tamaño de un puño.",
    "Read the scratches on the wall": "Leer las marcas de la pared",
    "Someone scratched a map into the stone, one passage circled twice. You copy it down.": "Alguien grabó un mapa en la piedra, con un pasadizo rodeado dos veces. Lo copias.",
    "The Robbed Traveller": "El viajero robado",
    "A man sits against the wall with his pack turned out beside him. His eyes are half shut. He sees you and tries to stand, and can't.\n\n\"There was a stand,\" he says. \"Soup. Nobody there.\" He laughs, and it turns into a yawn. \"They took everything.\"": "Un hombre está sentado contra la pared, con la mochila vaciada a su lado. Tiene los ojos medio cerrados. Te ve e intenta levantarse. No puede.\n\n«Había un puesto», dice. «Sopa. No había nadie». Se ríe, y la risa se convierte en bostezo. «Se lo llevaron todo».",
    "Give him your Antidote": "Darle tu Antídoto",
    "He drinks it in one go. After a while his eyes open properly and he sits up straight.\n\n": "Se lo bebe de un trago. Al rato abre bien los ojos y se endereza.\n\n",
    "He has nothing left to pay you with, except the one thing they missed. He unpicks his collar and puts it in your hand.": "No le queda nada con lo que pagarte, salvo lo único que se les pasó. Deshace la costura del cuello y te lo pone en la mano.",
    "He unpicks his collar to pay you, and finds it empty. He looks at you for a long time. \"Thank you,\" he says.": "Deshace la costura del cuello para pagarte. Está vacío. Te mira un buen rato. «Gracias», dice.",
    "Cast Restoration on him": "Lanzarle Restauración",
    "You hold the card over him. The light goes into him and he sits up straight.\n\n": "Sostienes la carta sobre él. La luz entra en su cuerpo y se endereza.\n\n",
    "Ask what happened": "Preguntar qué pasó",
    "\"Three of them. A stand, a pot.\" He yawns. \"Green scarves. I had one bowl and woke up like this. They took my antidotes.\"\n\nHe tells you where they sleep. It isn't far.": "«Eran tres. Un puesto, una olla». Bosteza. «Pañuelos verdes. Me tomé un cuenco y desperté así. Se llevaron mis antídotos».\n\nTe dice dónde duermen. No está lejos.",
    "Give him food": "Darle comida",
    "He eats, and perks up enough to talk.\n\n\"My purse is in the lining,\" he says, and tells you where the gang sleeps. Then he nods off again, smiling.": "Come y se anima lo suficiente para hablar.\n\n«Mi bolsa está en el forro», dice, y te cuenta dónde duerme la banda. Luego vuelve a dormirse, sonriendo.",
    "Search his pack": "Registrar su mochila",
    "There is a purse sewn into the lining. He watches you cut it out, too sleepy to stop you.\n\n\"Of course,\" he mumbles. \"Of course you would.\"": "Hay una bolsa cosida al forro. Te ve cortarla, demasiado adormilado para impedirlo.\n\n«Claro», murmura. «Claro que sí».",
    "You leave him dozing against the wall. He will wake up eventually.": "Lo dejas dormitando contra la pared. Ya se despertará.",
    "The Soup Stand": "El puesto de sopa",
    "A wooden stand against the wall. On it, a pot of soup, still steaming, a ladle and two clean bowls.\n\nYou call out. Nobody answers. You call again, louder. Nothing.": "Un puesto de madera contra la pared. Encima, una olla de sopa que aún humea, un cucharón y dos cuencos limpios.\n\nLlamas. Nadie responde. Llamas otra vez, más fuerte. Nada.",
    "Eat the soup": "Comer la sopa",
    "It is good soup. You have a second bowl.\n\nHalfway through it your fingers go numb, and you understand why nobody was minding the stand. Too late.\n\nWhen you wake up the pot is gone, and so is half your purse.": "La sopa está buena. Te sirves otro cuenco.\n\nA la mitad se te duermen los dedos, y entiendes por qué nadie atendía el puesto. Demasiado tarde.\n\nCuando despiertas, la olla ya no está. La mitad de tus monedas tampoco.",
    "Wait out of sight": "Esperar a escondidas",
    "You step behind the wall and wait. The soup goes on steaming.\n\nThree men in green scarves come back for it. The cook lifts his ladle, looks at the two clean bowls, then at your wall.": "Te escondes detrás de la pared y esperas. La sopa sigue humeando.\n\nTres hombres con pañuelos verdes vuelven a buscarla. El cocinero levanta el cucharón, mira los dos cuencos limpios y luego tu pared.",
    "Leave it and keep going": "Dejarla y seguir",
    "You leave the soup where it is and keep walking. Behind you it goes on steaming.": "Dejas la sopa donde está y sigues andando. A tu espalda sigue humeando.",
    "Kick the pot over": "Volcar la olla de una patada",
    "You kick the pot off the stand. Soup runs across the stones. The first rat to lick it falls asleep on the spot.\n\nThe stand tips over with it. Nailed to the underside is a purse: whatever the last few customers were carrying.\n\nYou take it and keep walking.": "De una patada tiras la olla del puesto. La sopa se extiende por las piedras. La primera rata que la lame se duerme en el acto.\n\nEl puesto también vuelca. Debajo hay una bolsa clavada: lo que llevaban los últimos clientes.\n\nLa coges y sigues andando.",
    "The Webbed Corridor": "El corredor de telarañas",
    "The corridor ahead is strung across with webs. The strands are thin and clear, and they catch the light like glass.\n\nSmall crystal spiders sit along them, a dozen at least, each about the size of your hand. The ones nearest you turn to watch.": "Las telarañas cruzan el corredor. Los hilos son finos y transparentes, y reflejan la luz como el vidrio.\n\nHay pequeñas arañas de cristal sobre ellos, al menos una docena, cada una del tamaño de tu mano. Las más cercanas se vuelven para mirarte.",
    "Cut through the webs": "Cortar las telarañas",
    "The first strand you cut rings like a wire.\n\nEvery spider on the web turns toward you at once.": "El primer hilo que cortas suena como un alambre.\n\nTodas las arañas de la telaraña se vuelven hacia ti a la vez.",
    "Go round through the rubble": "Rodear por los escombros",
    "There is a gap where the wall has fallen in. You squeeze through it on your stomach and come out bleeding from both elbows.\n\nA strand of web has caught on your sleeve. By the time you pick it off, it has gone hard and clear.": "Hay un hueco donde se ha derrumbado la pared. Pasas por él a rastras y sales con los dos codos sangrando.\n\nUn hilo de telaraña se ha enganchado en tu manga. Cuando lo quitas, ya está duro y transparente.",
    "Toss them some food": "Echarles algo de comida",
    "The food lands on the web and the nearest spiders are on it before it stops shaking.\n\nThe rest climb up out of the way. Where they were sitting, the web has left a few shards of crystal behind.": "La comida cae en la telaraña. Las arañas más cercanas ya están encima antes de que deje de temblar.\n\nLas demás trepan y dejan paso. Donde estaban, quedan unos fragmentos de cristal en la telaraña.",
    "Turn back": "Volver atrás",
    "You go back the way you came. Behind you, something ticks along the strands.": "Vuelves por donde viniste. A tu espalda, algo repiquetea por los hilos.",
    "The Silk Cache": "El escondite de seda",
    "The passage widens into a low chamber. Silk hangs in sheets from the ceiling, and beneath it the floor is crowded with pale cocoons — some the size of a fist, some large enough to hold a man.\n\nScattered between them: a buckled breastplate, a snapped spear, a glove still shaped around an empty hand. Someone fought here. Someone lost.\n\nThe cocoons twitch when you breathe too loud.": "El pasadizo se ensancha en una cámara de techo bajo. Del techo cuelgan mantos de seda. Debajo, el suelo está lleno de capullos pálidos: unos del tamaño de un puño, otros bastante grandes para un hombre.\n\nEntre ellos: una coraza abollada, una lanza partida, un guante que conserva la forma de una mano que ya no está. Alguien luchó aquí. Alguien perdió.\n\nLos capullos se mueven si respiras demasiado fuerte.",
    "Leave quietly": "Irte en silencio",
    "You ease back into the corridor without touching a strand.\n\nBehind you the silk settles, and the twitching stops.": "Retrocedes hasta el corredor sin tocar un solo hilo.\n\nA tu espalda, la seda se asienta y los capullos dejan de moverse.",
    "Search the cocoons": "Registrar los capullos",
    "You draw a blade and step into the silk.\n\nThe nearest cocoon does not open when you cut it — it resists, tough as wet leather. You will have to break them properly.": "Desenvainas y te adentras en la seda.\n\nEl capullo más cercano no se abre al cortarlo. Se resiste, duro como cuero mojado. Tendrás que romperlos de verdad.",
    "Burn them all!": "¡Quemarlos todos!",
    "The fireball takes the chamber in one breath.\n\nSilk blackens. Cocoons split and collapse. When the smoke thins, three scorched prizes lie open on the stone — and nothing moves to claim them.": "La bola de fuego llena la cámara de golpe.\n\nLa seda ennegrece. Los capullos se abren y se derrumban. Cuando el humo se disipa, quedan tres tesoros chamuscados sobre la piedra. Nada se mueve para reclamarlos.",
    "The Lost Porter": "El porteador perdido",
    "A side corridor has gone white with old web. Halfway along it, a man hangs upside down, wrapped to the armpits, holding a frying pan.\n\n\"Oh! Hello! Have you seen my party? They told me to hold the rope while they scouted ahead. So I held it.\"\n\nHe lifts the end of the rope. It has been cut clean through.\n\n\"Must have snapped. Anyway, I think I'm lost.\"": "Un corredor lateral está blanco de telarañas viejas. A medio camino cuelga un hombre boca abajo, envuelto hasta las axilas, con una sartén en la mano.\n\n«¡Oh! ¡Hola! ¿Has visto a mi grupo? Me dijeron que sujetara la cuerda mientras exploraban. Así que la sujeté».\n\nLevanta el extremo de la cuerda. El corte es limpio.\n\n«Se habrá roto. En fin, creo que me he perdido».",
    "Give him your spare armor": "Darle tu armadura de sobra",
    "You cut him down and help him into the armor. It is far too big. The helmet turns when he turns his head, a little after.\n\n\"It's like wearing a house,\" he says happily, and knocks on his own chest.": "Lo liberas y lo ayudas a ponerse la armadura. Le queda enorme. El casco gira cuando mueve la cabeza, un poco después.\n\n«Es como llevar una casa puesta», dice contento, y se da unos golpecitos en el pecho.",
    "Take the map": "Coger el mapa",
    "\"I don't think I'm cut out for adventuring,\" he says. \"Ma said so. I'm going home.\"\n\nHe presses the rolled map into your hands. \"I only carried it because I carry everything.\"\n\nIn one corner, in faded ink and a different hand, a passage is marked that you have never seen.\n\nHe clanks away down your cleared corridor, humming, frying pan first.": "«Creo que esto de las aventuras no es lo mío», dice. «Mamá ya me lo decía. Me voy a casa».\n\nTe pone el mapa enrollado en las manos. «Lo llevaba porque lo llevo todo».\n\nEn una esquina, con tinta desvaída y otra letra, está marcado un pasadizo que nunca has visto.\n\nSe aleja por el corredor que has despejado, tintineando y tarareando, con la sartén por delante.",
    "Give him a weapon": "Darle un arma",
    "You cut him down and put a weapon in his hands. He holds it like a broom.\n\n\"I'll just wave it if anything's scary. Things don't like being waved at. I bet.\"": "Lo liberas y le pones un arma en las manos. La sostiene como una escoba.\n\n«Si algo da miedo, la agito y ya está. A las cosas no les gusta que les agiten cosas delante. Seguro».",
    "Heal him": "Curarlo",
    "You cut him down. The web has left a red rash up both arms, and he has gone a little purple.\n\nHe drinks your potion, blinks twice, and bounces on his toes. \"Oh, that's much better. That's like breakfast.\"": "Lo liberas. La telaraña le ha dejado un sarpullido rojo en ambos brazos y se ha puesto algo morado.\n\nBebe tu poción, parpadea dos veces y da unos saltitos. «Ah, mucho mejor. Es como desayunar».",
    "Point the way and walk on": "Indicarle el camino y seguir",
    "You cut him down and point back the way you came. \"That way's safe. I already cleared it.\"\n\nHe shakes your hand with both of his. \"You're very kind. Everyone in this place is so kind.\"": "Lo liberas y señalas por donde viniste. «Por ahí es seguro. Ya lo despejé».\n\nTe estrecha la mano con las dos suyas. «Qué amable eres. Todos aquí son muy amables».",
    "Voices Around the Corner": "Voces a la vuelta de la esquina",
    "Three voices, low and angry, just past the next turn.\n\n\"You had the map.\" \"No, HE had the map. He carries everything.\" \"So go back and get it.\" \"Past the spider? You go back.\"\n\n\"We didn't lose him. We left him. That's different.\"\n\n\"Not to the map, it isn't.\"": "Tres voces, bajas y furiosas, justo tras la siguiente esquina.\n\n«Tú tenías el mapa». «No, lo tenía ÉL. Él lo lleva todo». «Pues vuelve a buscarlo». «¿Pasando por la araña? Ve tú».\n\n«No lo perdimos. Lo dejamos. No es lo mismo».\n\n«Para el mapa, sí».",
    "Sneak past": "Pasar a escondidas",
    "You keep to the far wall and step only on the silk, where it swallows the sound.\n\nThey are still arguing when you reach the next room. They never look up.": "Te pegas a la pared más alejada y pisas solo la seda, que amortigua el ruido.\n\nSiguen discutiendo cuando llegas a la siguiente sala. No levantan la vista.",
    "Confront them": "Encararte con ellos",
    "Three hands go to three weapons, then relax when they see you are alone.\n\n\"Your porter is fine,\" you say. \"He thinks he got lost.\"\n\nThey look at their boots. \"...Good,\" the leader mutters at last. \"Good for him.\"": "Tres manos van a tres armas. Luego se relajan al ver que estás solo.\n\n«Vuestro porteador está bien», dices. «Cree que se perdió».\n\nSe miran las botas. «...Bien», murmura al fin el jefe. «Bien por él».",
    "Give them back the map": "Devolverles el mapa",
    "The leader snatches the map and tucks it away as if it had never left.\n\nThen he pats you on the shoulder. Twice. The way you pat a dog that brought back a stick.\n\n\"Decent of you. Very decent. Off you go, then.\"": "El jefe te arrebata el mapa y lo guarda como si nunca hubiera faltado.\n\nLuego te da dos palmaditas en el hombro. Como a un perro que ha traído un palo.\n\n«Muy decente por tu parte. Muy decente. Hala, sigue tu camino».",
});
Object.assign(EVENT_NARRATIVE_TRANSLATIONS.fr, {
    "The Abandoned Camp": "Le camp abandonné",
    "A camp in a side chamber, left in a hurry. The fire is cold. The tent still stands, one pole leaning.\n\nBedrolls, a cooking pot, a bag half unpacked. Nobody came back for any of it.": "Un camp dans une salle latérale, abandonné à la hâte. Le feu est froid. La tente tient encore, un piquet de travers.\n\nDes couchages, une marmite, un sac à moitié défait. Personne n’est revenu chercher quoi que ce soit.",
    "Sleep in the tent": "Dormir dans la tente",
    "In the night, something walks around the tent. Then it stops walking.": "Dans la nuit, quelque chose marche autour de la tente. Puis cesse de marcher.",
    "You sleep. Nobody comes.\n\nIn the morning the camp is exactly as they left it.": "Vous dormez. Personne ne vient.\n\nAu matin, le camp est exactement comme ils l’ont laissé.",
    "Look around the camp": "Inspecter le camp",
    "Behind the tent, half under the bedrolls, you find one of them.\n\nHis sword is out of its sheath. The blade is clean. There is not a mark on him.\n\nHe did not die fighting. His face looks as if he saw a ghost.": "Derrière la tente, à moitié sous les couchages, vous trouvez l’un d’eux.\n\nSon épée est sortie du fourreau. La lame est propre. Il n’a pas une égratignure.\n\nIl n’est pas mort au combat. À voir son visage, on dirait qu’il a vu un fantôme.",
    "Take his backpack": "Prendre son sac",
    "You are still crouched over him when the tent flap moves behind you.\n\nThere is no wind down here.": "Vous êtes encore accroupi au-dessus de lui quand le pan de la tente bouge derrière vous.\n\nIl n’y a pas de vent ici.",
    "Nothing moves. You leave him the rest.": "Rien ne bouge. Vous lui laissez le reste.",
    "Take his sword": "Prendre son épée",
    "Take his armor": "Prendre son armure",
    "Bury him and pray": "L’enterrer et prier",
    "You leave his things where they are. The ground is soft enough.\n\nWhen you finish the prayer, the chamber is very quiet. You stand up lighter than you knelt down.": "Vous laissez ses affaires en place. La terre est assez meuble.\n\nQuand vous finissez la prière, la salle est très calme. Vous vous relevez plus léger qu’en vous agenouillant.",
    "Leave him": "Le laisser",
    "You leave him as you found him. You do not look at his face again.": "Vous le laissez comme vous l’avez trouvé. Vous ne regardez plus son visage.",
    "Leave the camp": "Quitter le camp",
    "You leave the camp as it is. Whoever left it is not coming back.": "Vous laissez le camp en l’état. Ceux qui l’ont quitté ne reviendront pas.",
    "A small black music box lies under the rubble — lid cracked, one brass leg twitching.\n\nAs you lean in, it plays three notes and snaps shut.": "Une petite boîte à musique noire gît sous les gravats : couvercle fendu, une patte en laiton qui tressaute.\n\nQuand vous vous penchez, elle joue trois notes et se referme d’un coup.",
    "Force it open": "Forcer le couvercle",
    "You pry at the lid.": "Vous faites levier sur le couvercle.",
    "Open it carefully": "L’ouvrir avec soin",
    "The lock gives. Inside, where the cylinder should turn, a cog is missing.\n\nThe box looks at you — somehow — then grows two more legs and falls in behind you.": "La serrure cède. À l’intérieur, là où le cylindre devrait tourner, il manque un rouage.\n\nLa boîte vous regarde. On ne sait comment. Puis deux autres pattes lui poussent et elle vous emboîte le pas.",
    "Leave it alone": "La laisser tranquille",
    "You step over it and keep walking.\n\nTen steps later: small metal feet on the stones behind you.": "Vous l’enjambez et continuez.\n\nDix pas plus loin : de petits pieds métalliques sur les pierres, derrière vous.",
    "A goblin steps out from behind a broken machine, sniffs the air, and coughs.\n\n": "Un gobelin sort de derrière une machine cassée, renifle l’air et tousse.\n\n",
    "\"Snatch Box. Charge went first. I can smell the powder from here. Nothing left to seat a cog in.\"\n\n": "« Boîte chapardeuse. La charge a sauté d’abord. Je sens la poudre d’ici. Plus rien où loger un rouage. »\n\n",
    "He looks at your boots as if a box might still be hiding there. It is not.": "Il regarde vos bottes comme si une boîte pouvait encore s’y cacher. Ce n’est pas le cas.",
    "A goblin steps out from behind a broken machine and points at the music box.\n\n\"Sleepy Snatch Box. Old robber model. Plays a song, puffs smoke, hero sleeps, pockets empty. Very illegal. Very profitable.\"\n\nThe box hides behind your boot.": "Un gobelin sort de derrière une machine cassée et montre la boîte à musique.\n\n« Boîte chapardeuse soporifique. Vieux modèle de brigand. Joue un air, souffle de la fumée, héros dort, poches vides. Très illégal. Très rentable. »\n\nLa boîte se cache derrière votre botte.",
    "\"You found its heart cog. Give it here — I can seat it properly. Or improperly. Depends on payment.\"": "« Vous avez trouvé son rouage central. Donnez, je peux le monter comme il faut. Ou pas. Ça dépend du paiement. »",
    "\"No cog? I have spares. Spare parts cost extra.\"": "« Pas de rouage ? J’ai des pièces de rechange. Les pièces, c’est en supplément. »",
    "Refuse to pay": "Refuser de payer",
    "Give him an unwanted card for spare parts": "Donner une carte à démonter",
    "Pay 30 coins for full repair": "Tout réparer : 30 pièces",
    "He shrugs. \"Ash is ash. I don't do funerals.\"\n\nHe is already back behind the machine before you turn away.": "Il hausse les épaules. « La cendre, c’est de la cendre. Je ne fais pas les enterrements. »\n\nIl est déjà retourné derrière la machine quand vous vous détournez.",
    "The Mirror Twin": "Le double du miroir",
    "A dry corner. You sit down and shut your eyes.\n\nWhen you open them, someone is sitting across from you. Hooded, cross-legged, wearing your face. The scar on your chin is on his other side.\n\nYou scratch your nose. He scratches his nose. His knees touch yours.": "Un coin sec. Vous vous asseyez et fermez les yeux.\n\nQuand vous les ouvrez, quelqu’un est assis en face. En capuche, les jambes croisées, avec votre visage. La cicatrice de votre menton est de l’autre côté du sien.\n\nVous vous grattez le nez. Il se gratte le nez. Ses genoux touchent les vôtres.",
    "Give him a shard": "Lui donner un éclat",
    "He holds the shard up. A face looks back from it, not yours. He turns to look closer.": "Il lève l’éclat. Un visage s’y reflète. Pas le vôtre. Il se tourne pour mieux voir.",
    "Sneak away": "Filer en douce",
    "You lift your pack one strap at a time and back out of the corner. He doesn't look up.\n\nOn the sixth step the floor stops.\n\nYou land on old rugs beside a dead camp. A note under a stone: \"Day 4. Mirror man STILL here. Going to try sneaking. Don't look back.\"\n\nUnder it, an amulet. You take it and climb out the far side. You don't look back.": "Vous soulevez votre sac, une bretelle après l’autre, et reculez hors du coin. Il ne lève pas les yeux.\n\nAu sixième pas, le sol s’arrête.\n\nVous atterrissez sur de vieux tapis près d’un camp désert. Un mot sous une pierre : « Jour 4. L’homme du miroir est TOUJOURS là. Vais essayer de filer en douce. Ne pas regarder derrière. »\n\nDessous, une amulette. Vous la prenez et remontez de l’autre côté. Vous ne regardez pas derrière.",
    "Give him the Gemseeker's Lens": "Donner la Lentille",
    "Even better: his own face, enormous. He presses his nose to it and forgets you.": "Encore mieux : son propre visage, énorme. Il y colle le nez et vous oublie.",
    "Give him the Hand Mirror": "Donner le Miroir à main",
    "He looks into the mirror. Another him looks back. He leans in. So does the other one.\n\nWhoosh.\n\nYou pick up the mirror. Your reflection isn't in it. He is, pressed flat against the glass, looking pleased.": "Il regarde dans le miroir. Un autre lui le regarde. Il s’approche. L’autre aussi.\n\nFrouf.\n\nVous ramassez le miroir. Votre reflet n’y est pas. Lui, si. Aplati contre la vitre, l’air content.",
    "Try to out-stare him": "Soutenir son regard",
    "You blink first. He does a small victory dance and wanders off, still dancing. You do not get your rest.": "Vous clignez des yeux en premier. Il fait une petite danse de victoire et s’en va, toujours en dansant. Vous n’avez pas eu votre repos.",
    "A shadow crosses the nest. Then again, lower.": "Une ombre passe sur le nid. Puis encore, plus bas.",
    "A nest sits wedged between two fallen pillars — speckled eggs, bent keys, old buttons, and one small brass cog.\n\n": "Un nid est coincé entre deux piliers tombés : des œufs tachetés, des clés tordues, de vieux boutons et un petit rouage en laiton.\n\n",
    "Search the nest": "Fouiller le nid",
    "You reach into the nest.": "Vous plongez la main dans le nid.",
    "The Old Chute": "La vieille chute",
    "A flagstone tips under your boot. You drop into an old trap chute and slide a long way down in the dark.\n\nWhatever was meant to be waiting at the bottom rotted away years ago. You land unhurt, on something that goes crack.\n\nUnder you is a spider the size of a dog, made of clear crystal. Most of it is in pieces now.": "Une dalle bascule sous votre botte. Vous tombez dans la chute d’un vieux piège et glissez longtemps dans le noir.\n\nCe qui devait vous attendre en bas a pourri il y a des années. Vous atterrissez sans mal sur quelque chose qui craque.\n\nSous vous, une araignée de la taille d’un chien, faite de cristal transparent. Elle est maintenant presque toute en morceaux.",
    "Take a crystal leg": "Prendre une patte de cristal",
    "One leg came off clean. It is cold, and it still catches the light.\n\nAhead of you, in the corner of the pit, is her nest: a heap of crystal eggs, each the size of a fist.": "Une patte s’est détachée net. Elle est froide et accroche encore la lumière.\n\nDevant vous, dans un coin de la fosse, son nid : un tas d’œufs de cristal, chacun gros comme le poing.",
    "Burn the eggs": "Brûler les œufs",
    "The fireball fills the pit. The eggs pop one by one.\n\nWhen the smoke clears, the heat has fused what is left into a single lump of crystal.": "La boule de feu remplit la fosse. Les œufs éclatent un par un.\n\nQuand la fumée se dissipe, la chaleur a soudé les restes en un seul bloc de cristal.",
    "Smash the eggs": "Briser les œufs",
    "The third egg is already open. So is the fourth.\n\nSmall crystal legs come out of the heap.": "Le troisième œuf est déjà ouvert. Le quatrième aussi.\n\nDe petites pattes de cristal sortent du tas.",
    "You crush them all. It is loud, and nothing answers.\n\nThe shards are worth something.": "Vous les écrasez tous. Cela fait du bruit. Rien ne répond.\n\nLes éclats valent quelque chose.",
    "Take one egg": "Prendre un œuf",
    "You pick the smallest one. It is cold, and heavier than it looks.\n\nSomething inside taps back.": "Vous prenez le plus petit. Il est froid, plus lourd qu’il n’y paraît.\n\nQuelque chose répond en tapotant de l’intérieur.",
    "Leave the nest": "Quitter le nid",
    "You leave the eggs where they are and climb out the long way.\n\nHalfway up, below you, one of them cracks.": "Vous laissez les œufs en place et remontez par le chemin le plus long.\n\nÀ mi-hauteur, sous vous, l’un d’eux se fend.",
    "Leave her be": "La laisser en paix",
    "You climb off her and leave her where she lies.\n\nAhead of you, in the corner of the pit, is her nest: a heap of crystal eggs, each the size of a fist.": "Vous vous dégagez et la laissez où elle est.\n\nDevant vous, dans un coin de la fosse, son nid : un tas d’œufs de cristal, chacun gros comme le poing.",
    "Read the scratches on the wall": "Lire les marques sur le mur",
    "Someone scratched a map into the stone, one passage circled twice. You copy it down.": "Quelqu’un a gravé une carte dans la pierre, un passage entouré deux fois. Vous la recopiez.",
    "The Robbed Traveller": "Le voyageur dépouillé",
    "A man sits against the wall with his pack turned out beside him. His eyes are half shut. He sees you and tries to stand, and can't.\n\n\"There was a stand,\" he says. \"Soup. Nobody there.\" He laughs, and it turns into a yawn. \"They took everything.\"": "Un homme est assis contre le mur, son sac vidé à côté de lui. Il a les yeux mi-clos. Il vous voit, essaie de se lever, n’y arrive pas.\n\n« Il y avait un étal, dit-il. De la soupe. Personne. » Il rit, puis son rire devient un bâillement. « Ils ont tout pris. »",
    "Give him your Antidote": "Lui donner votre Antidote",
    "He drinks it in one go. After a while his eyes open properly and he sits up straight.\n\n": "Il boit d’un trait. Au bout d’un moment, ses yeux s’ouvrent bien et il se redresse.\n\n",
    "He has nothing left to pay you with, except the one thing they missed. He unpicks his collar and puts it in your hand.": "Il n’a plus rien pour vous payer, sauf la seule chose qu’ils ont ratée. Il découd son col et vous la met dans la main.",
    "He unpicks his collar to pay you, and finds it empty. He looks at you for a long time. \"Thank you,\" he says.": "Il découd son col pour vous payer et le trouve vide. Il vous regarde longtemps. « Merci », dit-il.",
    "Cast Restoration on him": "Lancer Restauration sur lui",
    "You hold the card over him. The light goes into him and he sits up straight.\n\n": "Vous tenez la carte au-dessus de lui. La lumière entre en lui et il se redresse.\n\n",
    "Ask what happened": "Demander ce qui s’est passé",
    "\"Three of them. A stand, a pot.\" He yawns. \"Green scarves. I had one bowl and woke up like this. They took my antidotes.\"\n\nHe tells you where they sleep. It isn't far.": "« Ils étaient trois. Un étal, une marmite. » Il bâille. « Des foulards verts. J’ai pris un bol et je me suis réveillé comme ça. Ils ont pris mes antidotes. »\n\nIl vous dit où ils dorment. Ce n’est pas loin.",
    "Give him food": "Lui donner à manger",
    "He eats, and perks up enough to talk.\n\n\"My purse is in the lining,\" he says, and tells you where the gang sleeps. Then he nods off again, smiling.": "Il mange et reprend assez de forces pour parler.\n\n« Ma bourse est dans la doublure », dit-il, puis il vous indique où dort la bande. Il se rendort ensuite, le sourire aux lèvres.",
    "Search his pack": "Fouiller son sac",
    "There is a purse sewn into the lining. He watches you cut it out, too sleepy to stop you.\n\n\"Of course,\" he mumbles. \"Of course you would.\"": "Une bourse est cousue dans la doublure. Il vous regarde la découper, trop somnolent pour vous en empêcher.\n\n« Bien sûr, marmonne-t-il. Bien sûr que vous aussi. »",
    "You leave him dozing against the wall. He will wake up eventually.": "Vous le laissez somnoler contre le mur. Il finira par se réveiller.",
    "The Soup Stand": "L’étal de soupe",
    "A wooden stand against the wall. On it, a pot of soup, still steaming, a ladle and two clean bowls.\n\nYou call out. Nobody answers. You call again, louder. Nothing.": "Un étal en bois contre le mur. Dessus, une marmite de soupe encore fumante, une louche et deux bols propres.\n\nVous appelez. Personne ne répond. Vous rappelez, plus fort. Rien.",
    "Eat the soup": "Manger la soupe",
    "It is good soup. You have a second bowl.\n\nHalfway through it your fingers go numb, and you understand why nobody was minding the stand. Too late.\n\nWhen you wake up the pot is gone, and so is half your purse.": "La soupe est bonne. Vous prenez un deuxième bol.\n\nÀ la moitié, vos doigts s’engourdissent et vous comprenez pourquoi personne ne tenait l’étal. Trop tard.\n\nÀ votre réveil, la marmite a disparu. La moitié de votre bourse aussi.",
    "Wait out of sight": "Attendre à couvert",
    "You step behind the wall and wait. The soup goes on steaming.\n\nThree men in green scarves come back for it. The cook lifts his ladle, looks at the two clean bowls, then at your wall.": "Vous passez derrière le mur et attendez. La soupe continue de fumer.\n\nTrois hommes aux foulards verts reviennent la chercher. Le cuisinier lève sa louche, regarde les deux bols propres, puis votre mur.",
    "Leave it and keep going": "Laisser et continuer",
    "You leave the soup where it is and keep walking. Behind you it goes on steaming.": "Vous laissez la soupe en place et continuez. Derrière vous, elle fume toujours.",
    "Kick the pot over": "Renverser la marmite du pied",
    "You kick the pot off the stand. Soup runs across the stones. The first rat to lick it falls asleep on the spot.\n\nThe stand tips over with it. Nailed to the underside is a purse: whatever the last few customers were carrying.\n\nYou take it and keep walking.": "Vous faites tomber la marmite d’un coup de pied. La soupe coule sur les pierres. Le premier rat qui la lèche s’endort sur place.\n\nL’étal bascule aussi. Une bourse est clouée dessous : ce que portaient les derniers clients.\n\nVous la prenez et continuez.",
    "The Webbed Corridor": "Le couloir aux toiles",
    "The corridor ahead is strung across with webs. The strands are thin and clear, and they catch the light like glass.\n\nSmall crystal spiders sit along them, a dozen at least, each about the size of your hand. The ones nearest you turn to watch.": "Des toiles barrent le couloir devant vous. Leurs fils sont fins et transparents, et accrochent la lumière comme du verre.\n\nDe petites araignées de cristal y sont posées, une douzaine au moins, chacune de la taille de votre main. Les plus proches se tournent pour vous regarder.",
    "Cut through the webs": "Couper les toiles",
    "The first strand you cut rings like a wire.\n\nEvery spider on the web turns toward you at once.": "Le premier fil que vous coupez résonne comme du métal.\n\nToutes les araignées de la toile se tournent vers vous en même temps.",
    "Go round through the rubble": "Passer par les gravats",
    "There is a gap where the wall has fallen in. You squeeze through it on your stomach and come out bleeding from both elbows.\n\nA strand of web has caught on your sleeve. By the time you pick it off, it has gone hard and clear.": "Il y a une brèche là où le mur s’est effondré. Vous rampez à travers et ressortez les deux coudes en sang.\n\nUn fil de toile s’est accroché à votre manche. Le temps de l’enlever, il est devenu dur et transparent.",
    "Toss them some food": "Leur jeter de la nourriture",
    "The food lands on the web and the nearest spiders are on it before it stops shaking.\n\nThe rest climb up out of the way. Where they were sitting, the web has left a few shards of crystal behind.": "La nourriture tombe sur la toile. Les araignées les plus proches sont dessus avant qu’elle cesse de trembler.\n\nLes autres grimpent et libèrent le passage. Là où elles étaient, la toile a laissé quelques éclats de cristal.",
    "Turn back": "Faire demi-tour",
    "You go back the way you came. Behind you, something ticks along the strands.": "Vous repartez par où vous êtes venu. Derrière vous, quelque chose court sur les fils à petits clics.",
    "The Silk Cache": "La cache de soie",
    "The passage widens into a low chamber. Silk hangs in sheets from the ceiling, and beneath it the floor is crowded with pale cocoons — some the size of a fist, some large enough to hold a man.\n\nScattered between them: a buckled breastplate, a snapped spear, a glove still shaped around an empty hand. Someone fought here. Someone lost.\n\nThe cocoons twitch when you breathe too loud.": "Le passage s’élargit en une salle basse. Des nappes de soie pendent du plafond. Dessous, le sol est couvert de cocons pâles, certains gros comme le poing, d’autres assez grands pour un homme.\n\nEntre eux : un plastron déformé, une lance brisée, un gant qui garde la forme d’une main absente. Quelqu’un s’est battu ici. Quelqu’un a perdu.\n\nLes cocons tressaillent quand vous respirez trop fort.",
    "Leave quietly": "Partir sans bruit",
    "You ease back into the corridor without touching a strand.\n\nBehind you the silk settles, and the twitching stops.": "Vous reculez dans le couloir sans toucher un fil.\n\nDerrière vous, la soie retombe et les cocons cessent de tressaillir.",
    "Search the cocoons": "Fouiller les cocons",
    "You draw a blade and step into the silk.\n\nThe nearest cocoon does not open when you cut it — it resists, tough as wet leather. You will have to break them properly.": "Vous tirez une lame et entrez dans la soie.\n\nLe cocon le plus proche ne s’ouvre pas sous la lame. Il résiste, coriace comme du cuir mouillé. Il faudra vraiment les briser.",
    "Burn them all!": "Tous les brûler !",
    "The fireball takes the chamber in one breath.\n\nSilk blackens. Cocoons split and collapse. When the smoke thins, three scorched prizes lie open on the stone — and nothing moves to claim them.": "La boule de feu envahit la salle d’un coup.\n\nLa soie noircit. Les cocons se fendent et s’affaissent. Quand la fumée se dissipe, trois trésors roussis sont à découvert sur la pierre. Rien ne bouge pour les réclamer.",
    "The Lost Porter": "Le porteur perdu",
    "A side corridor has gone white with old web. Halfway along it, a man hangs upside down, wrapped to the armpits, holding a frying pan.\n\n\"Oh! Hello! Have you seen my party? They told me to hold the rope while they scouted ahead. So I held it.\"\n\nHe lifts the end of the rope. It has been cut clean through.\n\n\"Must have snapped. Anyway, I think I'm lost.\"": "Un couloir latéral est blanc de vieilles toiles. À mi-chemin, un homme pend la tête en bas, enveloppé jusqu’aux aisselles, une poêle à la main.\n\n« Oh ! Bonjour ! Vous avez vu mon groupe ? Ils m’ont dit de tenir la corde pendant qu’ils partaient en éclaireurs. Alors je l’ai tenue. »\n\nIl lève le bout de la corde. Elle a été coupée net.\n\n« Elle a dû casser. Enfin, je crois que je suis perdu. »",
    "Give him your spare armor": "Donner une armure en trop",
    "You cut him down and help him into the armor. It is far too big. The helmet turns when he turns his head, a little after.\n\n\"It's like wearing a house,\" he says happily, and knocks on his own chest.": "Vous le décrochez et l’aidez à enfiler l’armure. Elle est bien trop grande. Le casque tourne quand il tourne la tête, un peu après.\n\n« C’est comme porter une maison », dit-il, ravi, en frappant sur son torse.",
    "Take the map": "Prendre la carte",
    "\"I don't think I'm cut out for adventuring,\" he says. \"Ma said so. I'm going home.\"\n\nHe presses the rolled map into your hands. \"I only carried it because I carry everything.\"\n\nIn one corner, in faded ink and a different hand, a passage is marked that you have never seen.\n\nHe clanks away down your cleared corridor, humming, frying pan first.": "« Je ne crois pas être fait pour l’aventure, dit-il. Maman me l’avait dit. Je rentre. »\n\nIl vous met la carte roulée dans les mains. « Je la portais parce que je porte tout. »\n\nDans un coin, à l’encre passée et d’une autre main, un passage que vous n’avez jamais vu est indiqué.\n\nIl s’éloigne en ferraillant dans le couloir que vous avez dégagé, fredonnant, la poêle en avant.",
    "Give him a weapon": "Lui donner une arme",
    "You cut him down and put a weapon in his hands. He holds it like a broom.\n\n\"I'll just wave it if anything's scary. Things don't like being waved at. I bet.\"": "Vous le décrochez et lui mettez une arme dans les mains. Il la tient comme un balai.\n\n« Je l’agiterai si quelque chose fait peur. Les choses n’aiment pas qu’on agite des trucs devant elles. Je parie. »",
    "Heal him": "Le soigner",
    "You cut him down. The web has left a red rash up both arms, and he has gone a little purple.\n\nHe drinks your potion, blinks twice, and bounces on his toes. \"Oh, that's much better. That's like breakfast.\"": "Vous le décrochez. La toile lui a laissé des rougeurs sur les deux bras et il est devenu un peu violet.\n\nIl boit votre potion, cligne deux fois des yeux et sautille. « Oh, ça va bien mieux. C’est comme un petit-déjeuner. »",
    "Point the way and walk on": "Indiquer le chemin et partir",
    "You cut him down and point back the way you came. \"That way's safe. I already cleared it.\"\n\nHe shakes your hand with both of his. \"You're very kind. Everyone in this place is so kind.\"": "Vous le décrochez et montrez le chemin par lequel vous êtes venu. « Par là, c’est sûr. J’ai déjà dégagé le passage. »\n\nIl vous serre la main des deux siennes. « Vous êtes bien aimable. Tout le monde ici est si aimable. »",
    "Voices Around the Corner": "Des voix au tournant",
    "Three voices, low and angry, just past the next turn.\n\n\"You had the map.\" \"No, HE had the map. He carries everything.\" \"So go back and get it.\" \"Past the spider? You go back.\"\n\n\"We didn't lose him. We left him. That's different.\"\n\n\"Not to the map, it isn't.\"": "Trois voix basses et furieuses, juste après le prochain tournant.\n\n« C’est toi qui avais la carte. » « Non, c’est LUI. Il porte tout. » « Alors retourne la chercher. » « En passant devant l’araignée ? Vas-y, toi. »\n\n« On ne l’a pas perdu. On l’a laissé. C’est différent. »\n\n« Pas pour la carte. »",
    "Sneak past": "Passer en douce",
    "You keep to the far wall and step only on the silk, where it swallows the sound.\n\nThey are still arguing when you reach the next room. They never look up.": "Vous longez le mur opposé et ne marchez que sur la soie, qui étouffe les bruits.\n\nIls se disputent encore quand vous atteignez la salle suivante. Ils ne lèvent pas les yeux.",
    "Confront them": "Les confronter",
    "Three hands go to three weapons, then relax when they see you are alone.\n\n\"Your porter is fine,\" you say. \"He thinks he got lost.\"\n\nThey look at their boots. \"...Good,\" the leader mutters at last. \"Good for him.\"": "Trois mains se portent sur trois armes, puis se détendent en voyant que vous êtes seul.\n\n« Votre porteur va bien, dites-vous. Il pense s’être perdu. »\n\nIls regardent leurs bottes. « ...Bien, marmonne enfin le chef. Tant mieux pour lui. »",
    "Give them back the map": "Leur rendre la carte",
    "The leader snatches the map and tucks it away as if it had never left.\n\nThen he pats you on the shoulder. Twice. The way you pat a dog that brought back a stick.\n\n\"Decent of you. Very decent. Off you go, then.\"": "Le chef vous arrache la carte et la range comme si elle n’avait jamais disparu.\n\nPuis il vous tapote l’épaule. Deux fois. Comme on flatte un chien qui a rapporté un bâton.\n\n« C’est bien de votre part. Très bien. Allez, filez. »",
});
Object.assign(EVENT_NARRATIVE_TRANSLATIONS.ru, {
    "The Abandoned Camp": "Брошенный лагерь",
    "A camp in a side chamber, left in a hurry. The fire is cold. The tent still stands, one pole leaning.\n\nBedrolls, a cooking pot, a bag half unpacked. Nobody came back for any of it.": "Лагерь в боковой зале, брошенный в спешке. Костёр остыл. Палатка ещё стоит, одна стойка покосилась.\n\nСпальные мешки, котелок, наполовину разобранная сумка. Ни за чем не вернулись.",
    "Sleep in the tent": "Спать в палатке",
    "In the night, something walks around the tent. Then it stops walking.": "Ночью что-то ходит вокруг палатки. Потом перестаёт ходить.",
    "You sleep. Nobody comes.\n\nIn the morning the camp is exactly as they left it.": "Вы спите. Никто не приходит.\n\nУтром лагерь выглядит ровно так, как его оставили.",
    "Look around the camp": "Осмотреть лагерь",
    "Behind the tent, half under the bedrolls, you find one of them.\n\nHis sword is out of its sheath. The blade is clean. There is not a mark on him.\n\nHe did not die fighting. His face looks as if he saw a ghost.": "За палаткой, наполовину под спальными мешками, вы находите одного из них.\n\nМеч вынут из ножен. Клинок чистый. На теле ни царапины.\n\nОн умер не в бою. Лицо такое, будто он увидел призрака.",
    "Take his backpack": "Взять его рюкзак",
    "You are still crouched over him when the tent flap moves behind you.\n\nThere is no wind down here.": "Вы всё ещё сидите над ним на корточках, когда за спиной шевелится полог палатки.\n\nЗдесь внизу нет ветра.",
    "Nothing moves. You leave him the rest.": "Ничего не шевелится. Остальное вы ему оставляете.",
    "Take his sword": "Взять его меч",
    "Take his armor": "Взять его броню",
    "Bury him and pray": "Похоронить и помолиться",
    "You leave his things where they are. The ground is soft enough.\n\nWhen you finish the prayer, the chamber is very quiet. You stand up lighter than you knelt down.": "Вы оставляете его вещи на месте. Земля достаточно мягкая.\n\nКогда вы заканчиваете молитву, в зале очень тихо. Вы встаёте с колен. Стало легче.",
    "Leave him": "Оставить его",
    "You leave him as you found him. You do not look at his face again.": "Вы оставляете его как нашли. На лицо больше не смотрите.",
    "Leave the camp": "Уйти из лагеря",
    "You leave the camp as it is. Whoever left it is not coming back.": "Вы оставляете лагерь как есть. Кто бы его ни бросил, он не вернётся.",
    "A small black music box lies under the rubble — lid cracked, one brass leg twitching.\n\nAs you lean in, it plays three notes and snaps shut.": "Под обломками лежит маленькая чёрная музыкальная шкатулка. Крышка треснула, одна латунная ножка дёргается.\n\nВы наклоняетесь. Она играет три ноты и захлопывается.",
    "Force it open": "Вскрыть силой",
    "You pry at the lid.": "Вы поддеваете крышку.",
    "Open it carefully": "Открыть осторожно",
    "The lock gives. Inside, where the cylinder should turn, a cog is missing.\n\nThe box looks at you — somehow — then grows two more legs and falls in behind you.": "Замок поддаётся. Внутри, там, где должен вращаться валик, не хватает шестерёнки.\n\nШкатулка смотрит на вас. Каким-то образом. Потом отращивает ещё две ножки и пристраивается сзади.",
    "Leave it alone": "Не трогать",
    "You step over it and keep walking.\n\nTen steps later: small metal feet on the stones behind you.": "Вы перешагиваете через неё и идёте дальше.\n\nЧерез десять шагов: маленькие металлические ножки стучат по камням позади вас.",
    "A goblin steps out from behind a broken machine, sniffs the air, and coughs.\n\n": "Из-за сломанной машины выходит гоблин, принюхивается и кашляет.\n\n",
    "\"Snatch Box. Charge went first. I can smell the powder from here. Nothing left to seat a cog in.\"\n\n": "«Шкатулка-воровка. Заряд сработал первым. Порох отсюда чую. Шестерёнку уже некуда ставить».\n\n",
    "He looks at your boots as if a box might still be hiding there. It is not.": "Он смотрит на ваши сапоги, будто шкатулка ещё может там прятаться. Её там нет.",
    "A goblin steps out from behind a broken machine and points at the music box.\n\n\"Sleepy Snatch Box. Old robber model. Plays a song, puffs smoke, hero sleeps, pockets empty. Very illegal. Very profitable.\"\n\nThe box hides behind your boot.": "Из-за сломанной машины выходит гоблин и указывает на музыкальную шкатулку.\n\n«Сонная шкатулка-воровка. Старая разбойничья модель. Играет песенку, пускает дым, герой спит, карманы пусты. Очень незаконно. Очень прибыльно».\n\nШкатулка прячется за вашим сапогом.",
    "\"You found its heart cog. Give it here — I can seat it properly. Or improperly. Depends on payment.\"": "«Вы нашли её сердечную шестерёнку. Давайте сюда. Могу поставить как надо. Или как не надо. Смотря сколько заплатите».",
    "\"No cog? I have spares. Spare parts cost extra.\"": "«Нет шестерёнки? У меня есть запасные. Запчасти за отдельную плату».",
    "Refuse to pay": "Отказаться платить",
    "Give him an unwanted card for spare parts": "Отдать карту на запчасти",
    "Pay 30 coins for full repair": "Полный ремонт за 30 монет",
    "He shrugs. \"Ash is ash. I don't do funerals.\"\n\nHe is already back behind the machine before you turn away.": "Он пожимает плечами. «Пепел есть пепел. Похоронами не занимаюсь».\n\nВы ещё не отвернулись, а он уже снова за машиной.",
    "The Mirror Twin": "Зеркальный двойник",
    "A dry corner. You sit down and shut your eyes.\n\nWhen you open them, someone is sitting across from you. Hooded, cross-legged, wearing your face. The scar on your chin is on his other side.\n\nYou scratch your nose. He scratches his nose. His knees touch yours.": "Сухой угол. Вы садитесь и закрываете глаза.\n\nКогда вы их открываете, напротив кто-то сидит. В капюшоне, скрестив ноги, с вашим лицом. Шрам на подбородке у него с другой стороны.\n\nВы чешете нос. Он чешет нос. Его колени касаются ваших.",
    "Give him a shard": "Дать ему осколок",
    "He holds the shard up. A face looks back from it, not yours. He turns to look closer.": "Он поднимает осколок. Из него смотрит лицо. Не ваше. Он отворачивается, чтобы разглядеть поближе.",
    "Sneak away": "Тихо уйти",
    "You lift your pack one strap at a time and back out of the corner. He doesn't look up.\n\nOn the sixth step the floor stops.\n\nYou land on old rugs beside a dead camp. A note under a stone: \"Day 4. Mirror man STILL here. Going to try sneaking. Don't look back.\"\n\nUnder it, an amulet. You take it and climb out the far side. You don't look back.": "Вы поднимаете рюкзак за одну лямку, потом за другую и пятитесь из угла. Он не поднимает глаз.\n\nНа шестом шаге пол кончается.\n\nВы приземляетесь на старые ковры возле вымершего лагеря. Под камнем записка: «День 4. Зеркальный человек ВСЁ ЕЩЁ здесь. Попробую уйти тихо. Не оглядываться».\n\nПод ней амулет. Вы берёте его и выбираетесь с другой стороны. Не оглядываетесь.",
    "Give him the Gemseeker's Lens": "Дать Линзу искателя камней",
    "Even better: his own face, enormous. He presses his nose to it and forgets you.": "Ещё лучше: его собственное лицо, огромное. Он прижимает к ней нос и забывает о вас.",
    "Give him the Hand Mirror": "Дать Ручное зеркало",
    "He looks into the mirror. Another him looks back. He leans in. So does the other one.\n\nWhoosh.\n\nYou pick up the mirror. Your reflection isn't in it. He is, pressed flat against the glass, looking pleased.": "Он смотрит в зеркало. Оттуда смотрит ещё один он. Он наклоняется ближе. Другой тоже.\n\nФьюх.\n\nВы поднимаете зеркало. Вашего отражения в нём нет. Зато есть он, расплющенный по стеклу, с довольным видом.",
    "Try to out-stare him": "Переиграть его в гляделки",
    "You blink first. He does a small victory dance and wanders off, still dancing. You do not get your rest.": "Вы моргаете первым. Он исполняет маленький победный танец и уходит, всё ещё пританцовывая. Отдохнуть вам не удалось.",
    "A shadow crosses the nest. Then again, lower.": "Над гнездом проходит тень. Потом ещё раз, ниже.",
    "A nest sits wedged between two fallen pillars — speckled eggs, bent keys, old buttons, and one small brass cog.\n\n": "Между двумя упавшими колоннами застряло гнездо. Пятнистые яйца, гнутые ключи, старые пуговицы и одна маленькая латунная шестерёнка.\n\n",
    "Search the nest": "Обыскать гнездо",
    "You reach into the nest.": "Вы запускаете руку в гнездо.",
    "The Old Chute": "Старый спуск",
    "A flagstone tips under your boot. You drop into an old trap chute and slide a long way down in the dark.\n\nWhatever was meant to be waiting at the bottom rotted away years ago. You land unhurt, on something that goes crack.\n\nUnder you is a spider the size of a dog, made of clear crystal. Most of it is in pieces now.": "Плита под сапогом наклоняется. Вы падаете в спуск старой ловушки и долго скользите вниз в темноте.\n\nВсё, что должно было ждать внизу, сгнило много лет назад. Вы приземляетесь без ушибов. Под вами что-то хрустит.\n\nЭто паучиха размером с собаку, из прозрачного кристалла. Теперь почти вся разбита.",
    "Take a crystal leg": "Взять кристальную лапу",
    "One leg came off clean. It is cold, and it still catches the light.\n\nAhead of you, in the corner of the pit, is her nest: a heap of crystal eggs, each the size of a fist.": "Одна лапа отломилась целиком. Холодная, всё ещё ловит свет.\n\nВпереди, в углу ямы, её гнездо: куча кристальных яиц, каждое с кулак.",
    "Burn the eggs": "Сжечь яйца",
    "The fireball fills the pit. The eggs pop one by one.\n\nWhen the smoke clears, the heat has fused what is left into a single lump of crystal.": "Огненный шар заполняет яму. Яйца лопаются одно за другим.\n\nКогда дым рассеивается, видно, что жар сплавил остатки в одну глыбу кристалла.",
    "Smash the eggs": "Разбить яйца",
    "The third egg is already open. So is the fourth.\n\nSmall crystal legs come out of the heap.": "Третье яйцо уже открыто. Четвёртое тоже.\n\nИз кучи тянутся маленькие кристальные лапки.",
    "You crush them all. It is loud, and nothing answers.\n\nThe shards are worth something.": "Вы давите их все. Шумно. Ничего не отзывается.\n\nОсколки чего-то стоят.",
    "Take one egg": "Взять одно яйцо",
    "You pick the smallest one. It is cold, and heavier than it looks.\n\nSomething inside taps back.": "Вы выбираете самое маленькое. Холодное и тяжелее, чем кажется.\n\nЧто-то внутри стучит в ответ.",
    "Leave the nest": "Уйти от гнезда",
    "You leave the eggs where they are and climb out the long way.\n\nHalfway up, below you, one of them cracks.": "Вы оставляете яйца на месте и выбираетесь долгим путём.\n\nНа полпути наверх внизу трескается одно из яиц.",
    "Leave her be": "Не трогать её",
    "You climb off her and leave her where she lies.\n\nAhead of you, in the corner of the pit, is her nest: a heap of crystal eggs, each the size of a fist.": "Вы слезаете с неё и оставляете лежать на месте.\n\nВпереди, в углу ямы, её гнездо: куча кристальных яиц, каждое с кулак.",
    "Read the scratches on the wall": "Прочесть царапины на стене",
    "Someone scratched a map into the stone, one passage circled twice. You copy it down.": "Кто-то выцарапал на камне карту. Один проход обведён дважды. Вы её срисовываете.",
    "The Robbed Traveller": "Ограбленный путник",
    "A man sits against the wall with his pack turned out beside him. His eyes are half shut. He sees you and tries to stand, and can't.\n\n\"There was a stand,\" he says. \"Soup. Nobody there.\" He laughs, and it turns into a yawn. \"They took everything.\"": "У стены сидит человек. Рядом вывернутый рюкзак. Глаза полузакрыты. Он видит вас, пытается встать и не может.\n\n«Там был прилавок, — говорит он. — Суп. Никого». Он смеётся, и смех переходит в зевок. «Всё забрали».",
    "Give him your Antidote": "Дать ему Противоядие",
    "He drinks it in one go. After a while his eyes open properly and he sits up straight.\n\n": "Он выпивает всё разом. Через некоторое время глаза открываются как следует, и он выпрямляется.\n\n",
    "He has nothing left to pay you with, except the one thing they missed. He unpicks his collar and puts it in your hand.": "Ему нечем заплатить, кроме одной вещи, которую они не нашли. Он распарывает воротник и кладёт её вам в ладонь.",
    "He unpicks his collar to pay you, and finds it empty. He looks at you for a long time. \"Thank you,\" he says.": "Он распарывает воротник, чтобы заплатить вам, но там пусто. Долго смотрит на вас. «Спасибо», — говорит он.",
    "Cast Restoration on him": "Применить Восстановление",
    "You hold the card over him. The light goes into him and he sits up straight.\n\n": "Вы держите над ним карту. Свет входит в него, и он выпрямляется.\n\n",
    "Ask what happened": "Спросить, что случилось",
    "\"Three of them. A stand, a pot.\" He yawns. \"Green scarves. I had one bowl and woke up like this. They took my antidotes.\"\n\nHe tells you where they sleep. It isn't far.": "«Трое. Прилавок, котелок». Он зевает. «Зелёные шарфы. Съел миску и проснулся вот так. Забрали мои противоядия».\n\nОн говорит, где они ночуют. Это недалеко.",
    "Give him food": "Дать ему еды",
    "He eats, and perks up enough to talk.\n\n\"My purse is in the lining,\" he says, and tells you where the gang sleeps. Then he nods off again, smiling.": "Он ест и оживает настолько, чтобы заговорить.\n\n«Кошелёк в подкладке», — говорит он и рассказывает, где ночует банда. Потом снова засыпает с улыбкой.",
    "Search his pack": "Обыскать его рюкзак",
    "There is a purse sewn into the lining. He watches you cut it out, too sleepy to stop you.\n\n\"Of course,\" he mumbles. \"Of course you would.\"": "В подкладку вшит кошелёк. Он смотрит, как вы его вырезаете. Слишком сонный, чтобы помешать.\n\n«Ну конечно, — бормочет он. — Кто бы сомневался».",
    "You leave him dozing against the wall. He will wake up eventually.": "Вы оставляете его дремать у стены. Когда-нибудь проснётся.",
    "The Soup Stand": "Прилавок с супом",
    "A wooden stand against the wall. On it, a pot of soup, still steaming, a ladle and two clean bowls.\n\nYou call out. Nobody answers. You call again, louder. Nothing.": "Деревянный прилавок у стены. На нём котелок с ещё дымящимся супом, половник и две чистые миски.\n\nВы зовёте. Никто не отвечает. Зовёте снова, громче. Ничего.",
    "Eat the soup": "Съесть суп",
    "It is good soup. You have a second bowl.\n\nHalfway through it your fingers go numb, and you understand why nobody was minding the stand. Too late.\n\nWhen you wake up the pot is gone, and so is half your purse.": "Суп хороший. Вы берёте вторую миску.\n\nНа середине немеют пальцы, и вы понимаете, почему за прилавком никого не было. Слишком поздно.\n\nКогда вы просыпаетесь, котелка уже нет. Половины денег тоже.",
    "Wait out of sight": "Подождать в укрытии",
    "You step behind the wall and wait. The soup goes on steaming.\n\nThree men in green scarves come back for it. The cook lifts his ladle, looks at the two clean bowls, then at your wall.": "Вы заходите за стену и ждёте. Суп всё дымится.\n\nЗа ним возвращаются трое мужчин в зелёных шарфах. Повар поднимает половник, смотрит на две чистые миски, потом на вашу стену.",
    "Leave it and keep going": "Оставить и идти дальше",
    "You leave the soup where it is and keep walking. Behind you it goes on steaming.": "Вы оставляете суп на месте и идёте дальше. Позади он всё дымится.",
    "Kick the pot over": "Опрокинуть котелок ногой",
    "You kick the pot off the stand. Soup runs across the stones. The first rat to lick it falls asleep on the spot.\n\nThe stand tips over with it. Nailed to the underside is a purse: whatever the last few customers were carrying.\n\nYou take it and keep walking.": "Вы сбиваете котелок с прилавка ногой. Суп растекается по камням. Первая крыса, лизнувшая его, тут же засыпает.\n\nПрилавок тоже опрокидывается. Снизу прибит кошелёк: всё, что было при последних посетителях.\n\nВы берёте его и идёте дальше.",
    "The Webbed Corridor": "Коридор в паутине",
    "The corridor ahead is strung across with webs. The strands are thin and clear, and they catch the light like glass.\n\nSmall crystal spiders sit along them, a dozen at least, each about the size of your hand. The ones nearest you turn to watch.": "Коридор впереди затянут паутиной. Нити тонкие и прозрачные, ловят свет, как стекло.\n\nНа них сидят маленькие кристальные пауки. Не меньше дюжины, каждый с вашу ладонь. Ближайшие поворачиваются к вам.",
    "Cut through the webs": "Прорубиться сквозь паутину",
    "The first strand you cut rings like a wire.\n\nEvery spider on the web turns toward you at once.": "Первая разрезанная нить звенит, как проволока.\n\nВсе пауки на паутине разом поворачиваются к вам.",
    "Go round through the rubble": "Обойти через завалы",
    "There is a gap where the wall has fallen in. You squeeze through it on your stomach and come out bleeding from both elbows.\n\nA strand of web has caught on your sleeve. By the time you pick it off, it has gone hard and clear.": "Там, где обвалилась стена, есть щель. Вы протискиваетесь на животе и вылезаете с ободранными до крови локтями.\n\nЗа рукав зацепилась паутинка. Пока вы её снимаете, она твердеет и становится прозрачной.",
    "Toss them some food": "Бросить им еды",
    "The food lands on the web and the nearest spiders are on it before it stops shaking.\n\nThe rest climb up out of the way. Where they were sitting, the web has left a few shards of crystal behind.": "Еда падает в паутину. Та ещё дрожит, а ближайшие пауки уже облепили еду.\n\nОстальные лезут наверх, освобождая путь. Там, где они сидели, паутина оставила несколько кристальных осколков.",
    "Turn back": "Повернуть назад",
    "You go back the way you came. Behind you, something ticks along the strands.": "Вы возвращаетесь тем же путём. Сзади что-то цокает по нитям.",
    "The Silk Cache": "Тайник в паутине",
    "The passage widens into a low chamber. Silk hangs in sheets from the ceiling, and beneath it the floor is crowded with pale cocoons — some the size of a fist, some large enough to hold a man.\n\nScattered between them: a buckled breastplate, a snapped spear, a glove still shaped around an empty hand. Someone fought here. Someone lost.\n\nThe cocoons twitch when you breathe too loud.": "Проход расширяется в залу с низким потолком. С потолка полотнищами свисает паутина. Под ней пол усеян бледными коконами: одни с кулак, в других поместится человек.\n\nМежду ними: смятая кираса, сломанное копьё, перчатка, всё ещё хранящая форму руки, которой в ней нет. Здесь кто-то сражался. Кто-то проиграл.\n\nКоконы дёргаются, когда вы дышите слишком громко.",
    "Leave quietly": "Тихо уйти",
    "You ease back into the corridor without touching a strand.\n\nBehind you the silk settles, and the twitching stops.": "Вы осторожно отступаете в коридор, не задев ни нити.\n\nПозади паутина оседает, и коконы перестают дёргаться.",
    "Search the cocoons": "Обыскать коконы",
    "You draw a blade and step into the silk.\n\nThe nearest cocoon does not open when you cut it — it resists, tough as wet leather. You will have to break them properly.": "Вы обнажаете клинок и входите в паутину.\n\nБлижайший кокон не раскрывается под лезвием. Он не поддаётся, прочный, как мокрая кожа. Придётся разбивать их всерьёз.",
    "Burn them all!": "Сжечь всё!",
    "The fireball takes the chamber in one breath.\n\nSilk blackens. Cocoons split and collapse. When the smoke thins, three scorched prizes lie open on the stone — and nothing moves to claim them.": "Огненный шар разом заполняет залу.\n\nПаутина чернеет. Коконы лопаются и оседают. Когда дым редеет, на камнях лежат три обгорелые награды. Никто не шевелится, чтобы их забрать.",
    "The Lost Porter": "Заблудившийся носильщик",
    "A side corridor has gone white with old web. Halfway along it, a man hangs upside down, wrapped to the armpits, holding a frying pan.\n\n\"Oh! Hello! Have you seen my party? They told me to hold the rope while they scouted ahead. So I held it.\"\n\nHe lifts the end of the rope. It has been cut clean through.\n\n\"Must have snapped. Anyway, I think I'm lost.\"": "Боковой коридор побелел от старой паутины. На полпути висит вниз головой человек, обмотанный до подмышек, со сковородкой в руке.\n\n«О! Здравствуйте! Вы моих не видели? Велели держать верёвку, пока они всё разведают впереди. Ну я и держал».\n\nОн поднимает конец верёвки. Она ровно перерезана.\n\n«Наверное, порвалась. В общем, кажется, я заблудился».",
    "Give him your spare armor": "Дать ему запасную броню",
    "You cut him down and help him into the armor. It is far too big. The helmet turns when he turns his head, a little after.\n\n\"It's like wearing a house,\" he says happily, and knocks on his own chest.": "Вы срезаете его и помогаете надеть броню. Она ему совсем велика. Шлем поворачивается вслед за головой. С небольшим опозданием.\n\n«Будто дом надел», — радуется он и стучит себя по груди.",
    "Take the map": "Взять карту",
    "\"I don't think I'm cut out for adventuring,\" he says. \"Ma said so. I'm going home.\"\n\nHe presses the rolled map into your hands. \"I only carried it because I carry everything.\"\n\nIn one corner, in faded ink and a different hand, a passage is marked that you have never seen.\n\nHe clanks away down your cleared corridor, humming, frying pan first.": "«Не гожусь я, кажется, в искатели приключений, — говорит он. — Мама так и говорила. Пойду домой».\n\nОн суёт вам в руки свёрнутую карту. «Я её носил, потому что я всё ношу».\n\nВ углу выцветшими чернилами и другим почерком отмечен проход, которого вы никогда не видели.\n\nОн с лязгом уходит по расчищенному вами коридору, напевая и выставив вперёд сковородку.",
    "Give him a weapon": "Дать ему оружие",
    "You cut him down and put a weapon in his hands. He holds it like a broom.\n\n\"I'll just wave it if anything's scary. Things don't like being waved at. I bet.\"": "Вы срезаете его и даёте в руки оружие. Он держит его как метлу.\n\n«Если будет что-то страшное, я просто помашу. Никому не нравится, когда перед ним машут. Наверное».",
    "Heal him": "Вылечить его",
    "You cut him down. The web has left a red rash up both arms, and he has gone a little purple.\n\nHe drinks your potion, blinks twice, and bounces on his toes. \"Oh, that's much better. That's like breakfast.\"": "Вы срезаете его. От паутины обе руки покрылись красной сыпью, а сам он слегка посинел.\n\nОн пьёт ваше зелье, дважды моргает и подпрыгивает на носках. «О, вот теперь гораздо лучше. Прямо как позавтракал».",
    "Point the way and walk on": "Указать дорогу и идти дальше",
    "You cut him down and point back the way you came. \"That way's safe. I already cleared it.\"\n\nHe shakes your hand with both of his. \"You're very kind. Everyone in this place is so kind.\"": "Вы срезаете его и указываете туда, откуда пришли. «Там безопасно. Я уже всё зачистил».\n\nОн пожимает вашу руку обеими руками. «Вы очень добры. Все здесь такие добрые».",
    "Voices Around the Corner": "Голоса за углом",
    "Three voices, low and angry, just past the next turn.\n\n\"You had the map.\" \"No, HE had the map. He carries everything.\" \"So go back and get it.\" \"Past the spider? You go back.\"\n\n\"We didn't lose him. We left him. That's different.\"\n\n\"Not to the map, it isn't.\"": "Три голоса, тихих и злых, сразу за следующим поворотом.\n\n«Карта была у тебя». «Нет, у НЕГО. Он всё таскает». «Ну так вернись и забери». «Мимо паука? Сам возвращайся».\n\n«Мы его не потеряли. Мы его оставили. Это другое».\n\n«Карте от этого не легче».",
    "Sneak past": "Прокрасться мимо",
    "You keep to the far wall and step only on the silk, where it swallows the sound.\n\nThey are still arguing when you reach the next room. They never look up.": "Вы держитесь дальней стены и ступаете только по паутине: она глушит шаги.\n\nКогда вы добираетесь до следующей комнаты, они всё ещё спорят. Так и не подняли глаз.",
    "Confront them": "Выйти к ним",
    "Three hands go to three weapons, then relax when they see you are alone.\n\n\"Your porter is fine,\" you say. \"He thinks he got lost.\"\n\nThey look at their boots. \"...Good,\" the leader mutters at last. \"Good for him.\"": "Три руки тянутся к оружию, потом расслабляются: вы один.\n\n«Ваш носильщик в порядке, — говорите вы. — Думает, что заблудился».\n\nОни смотрят на свои сапоги. «...Хорошо, — наконец бормочет главарь. — Хорошо ему».",
    "Give them back the map": "Вернуть им карту",
    "The leader snatches the map and tucks it away as if it had never left.\n\nThen he pats you on the shoulder. Twice. The way you pat a dog that brought back a stick.\n\n\"Decent of you. Very decent. Off you go, then.\"": "Главарь выхватывает карту и прячет её, словно она никуда и не девалась.\n\nПотом хлопает вас по плечу. Дважды. Как пса, который принёс палку.\n\n«Порядочно с вашей стороны. Очень порядочно. Ну, ступайте».",
});
// <<< imported stories-translated.json

// >>> imported stories-runtime-translated.json (tools/import-translations.mjs)
Object.assign(EVENT_NARRATIVE_TRANSLATIONS.es, {
    "You push the gem past the teeth. It rolls up into an eye socket and fits exactly.\n\nRed light spreads through the cracks in the face. The head exhales one slow cloud of dust — and when it clears, a Fire Rune is resting on the stone tongue.": "Empujas la gema entre los dientes. Rueda hasta una cuenca y encaja perfectamente.\n\nUna luz roja se extiende por las grietas de la cara. La cabeza exhala una lenta nube de polvo. Cuando se disipa, hay una Runa de fuego sobre la lengua de piedra.",
    "You push the gem past the teeth. It clicks into an eye socket.\n\nA thin bolt skips across the cracked forehead, and the teeth chatter once. The head exhales dust — and a Lightning Rune flickers between its teeth.": "Empujas la gema entre los dientes. Encaja con un chasquido en una cuenca.\n\nUn rayo fino recorre la frente agrietada y los dientes castañetean una vez. La cabeza exhala polvo. Una Runa de rayo parpadea entre sus dientes.",
    "You push the gem past the teeth. It settles into an eye socket.\n\nGreen light seeps through the cracks, and the mouth curls — almost like remembering pain. The head exhales a bitter cloud. Behind it, a dark green rune rests on the stone tongue.": "Empujas la gema entre los dientes. Se asienta en una cuenca.\n\nUna luz verde se filtra por las grietas y la boca se tuerce, casi como si recordara un dolor. La cabeza exhala una nube amarga. Detrás queda una runa verde oscura sobre la lengua de piedra.",
    "You set the Crystal Spiderling card down on the cracked floor of the drill room.\n\nThe spiderling climbs off the card, taps along the cracks and pulls a grain of crystal out of one.\n\nIt climbs back into the picture and keeps the grain.": "Pones la carta de la Arañita de cristal en el suelo agrietado de la sala de entrenamiento.\n\nLa arañita sale de la carta, tantea las grietas y saca de una un grano de cristal.\n\nVuelve a la imagen y se queda con el grano.",
    "You slide the card between the stone teeth.\n\nThe mouth closes. Stone grinds on stone, and for a few seconds the head chews.\n\nThen the jaw cracks open. A different card is lying on the tongue, damp with gray dust.": "Deslizas la carta entre los dientes de piedra.\n\nLa boca se cierra. La piedra rechina contra la piedra y la cabeza mastica unos segundos.\n\nLuego la mandíbula se abre con un crujido. Sobre la lengua hay otra carta, húmeda de polvo gris.",
    "You hold the card out to the vines.\n\nThey wrap it carefully — almost gently — and sink a few black thorns into its edge.\n\nWhen they let go, the card is not the same.": "Tiendes la carta hacia las enredaderas.\n\nLa envuelven con cuidado, casi con suavidad, y clavan unas espinas negras en el borde.\n\nCuando la sueltan, la carta ya no es la misma.",
    "A few of them stop chewing when they see what you are carrying. One goblin quietly moves round to your side of the table.": "Algunos dejan de masticar al ver lo que llevas. Un goblin pasa discretamente a tu lado de la mesa.",
    "Nobody moves. The thing with too many legs watches both of you and does not pick a side.": "Nadie se mueve. La cosa con demasiadas patas os mira a los dos y no toma partido.",
    "The whole room is already laughing. Someone starts collecting bets before you have sat down.": "Toda la sala ya se está riendo. Alguien empieza a recoger apuestas antes de que te sientes.",
    "He is stronger than you and both of you know it, so you do not try to out-pull him. You wait until he leans, and then you stop being where he is pushing.\n\nHis own weight takes his hand down onto the slab.\n\nThe room goes very quiet. The ogre looks at his hand for a while, then at you, and pushes the whole stack of coins across the table without a word.": "Es más fuerte que tú y ambos lo sabéis, así que no intentas ganarle por fuerza. Esperas a que se incline y dejas de estar donde él empuja.\n\nSu propio peso lleva su mano contra la losa.\n\nLa sala se queda en silencio. El ogro mira su mano un rato, luego te mira a ti y te empuja todo el montón de monedas sin decir nada.",
    "You get about two seconds of holding him.\n\nThen your knuckles find the stone.\n\nHe takes the coins. That is all he takes.": "Aguantas unos dos segundos.\n\nLuego tus nudillos encuentran la piedra.\n\nSe lleva las monedas. Solo se lleva eso.",
    "He goes at it properly this time, and it takes everything you have.\n\nWhen his hand finally goes down the crowd does not cheer. They just look at the ogre.\n\nHe unhooks the stone guard and pushes it across to you, then sits back with his arms folded and watches you take it, {card} and all.": "Esta vez va en serio y necesitas todo lo que tienes.\n\nCuando su mano por fin cae, el público no aplaude. Solo mira al ogro.\n\nSe desabrocha el protector de piedra y te lo empuja. Luego se reclina con los brazos cruzados y te ve recogerlo todo, incluida tu carta: {card}.",
    "He looks at {card} for a long moment, decides it is worth his time, and plants his elbow.\n\nYou win by not fighting him where he is strongest.\n\nHe pushes his coins over, keeps looking at his own hand, and says something short in Ogrish. The crowd stops laughing. You get the distinct impression this is not finished.": "Mira la carta, {card}, un buen rato, decide que merece su tiempo y planta el codo.\n\nGanas evitando medir fuerzas donde él tiene ventaja.\n\nTe empuja sus monedas, sigue mirándose la mano y dice algo breve en ogresco. El público deja de reír. Te queda muy claro que esto no ha terminado.",
    "He does not make the same mistake twice.\n\nYour hand is on the slab before you have finished bracing, and {card} goes into the pile beside his elbow.\n\nHe buckles the stone guard back onto his forearm and turns away from the table.": "No comete el mismo error dos veces.\n\nTu mano ya está contra la losa cuando aún intentas afirmarte, y tu carta, {card}, va al montón junto a su codo.\n\nSe abrocha el protector de piedra en el antebrazo y se aparta de la mesa.",
    "He takes {card} off the table before your hand has finished going down.\n\nThe crowd is delighted, briefly, and then bored.": "Se lleva tu carta, {card}, antes de que tu mano termine de caer.\n\nEl público se entusiasma un momento. Luego se aburre.",
    "You do not say anything. You draw the weapon and rest it against the doors, in the light, where all three of them can see it properly.\n\nThe one with the tally board stops writing. The one with the shield finds something interesting on the floor.\n\nNobody stops you lifting the lid of the strongbox at the foot of the door, and nobody looks at you either. The bar is already off by the time you straighten up.": "No dices nada. Sacas el arma y la apoyas contra las puertas, a la luz, donde los tres puedan verla bien.\n\nEl de la tablilla deja de escribir. El del escudo encuentra algo interesante en el suelo.\n\nNadie te impide abrir el cofre al pie de la puerta. Nadie te mira tampoco. Cuando te enderezas, ya han quitado la tranca.",
    "You press the weapon flat against the glass.\n\nThe case opens from the inside. The {magic} settles against the metal and sinks in, and the glass closes over nothing.\n\nThe other cases go dark.\n\nWhat you are holding is called {weapon} now.": "Apoyas el arma plana contra el cristal.\n\nLa vitrina se abre desde dentro. La carta, {magic}, se posa sobre el metal y se hunde en él. El cristal se cierra sobre el vacío.\n\nLas otras vitrinas se oscurecen.\n\nLo que tienes en las manos ahora se llama {weapon}.",
    "You put your elbow through the nearest case.\n\nThe glass opens your arm. Whatever was inside is already gone.": "Rompes la vitrina más cercana con el codo.\n\nEl cristal te abre el brazo. Lo que había dentro ya no está.",
    "You put your elbow through the case holding the {magic}.\n\nThe ward goes off late and shallow, opening a line across your forearm — but the card is in your fist and it stays there.\n\nThe remaining cases go dark before the glass finishes falling.": "Rompes con el codo la vitrina que contiene la carta: {magic}.\n\nLa protección se activa tarde y apenas te abre un corte en el antebrazo. Pero la carta está en tu puño y ahí se queda.\n\nLas demás vitrinas se oscurecen antes de que el cristal termine de caer.",
    "You hold the card out over the water. Your reflection lifts the wrong hand.\n\nThe card sinks without a sound. A different one comes up, cold and dripping tar.\n\nFor a second it feels like you made a deal with yourself.": "Tiendes la carta sobre el agua. Tu reflejo levanta la mano equivocada.\n\nLa carta se hunde sin hacer ruido. Sube otra distinta, fría y goteando alquitrán.\n\nPor un segundo parece que has hecho un trato contigo mismo.",
    "You put the trinket on the tray. It snaps back into the booth.\n\nThe glass goes dark. Then a rainbow sheen spreads across it from the inside — thin and oily, like light on spilled ink.\n\nA card slides out. It is far too bright for the machine that made it.": "Pones la baratija en la bandeja. Se recoge de golpe dentro de la cabina.\n\nEl cristal se oscurece. Luego un brillo arcoíris se extiende por dentro, fino y aceitoso, como luz sobre tinta derramada.\n\nSale una carta. Es demasiado brillante para la máquina que la ha hecho.",
    "You put one of your cards on the tray. It snaps back before you can change your mind.\n\nBehind the glass, the wizard looks at the card for a long time. Then it taps the glass twice.\n\nA different card slides out.": "Pones una de tus cartas en la bandeja. Se recoge antes de que puedas cambiar de idea.\n\nTras el cristal, el mago mira la carta un buen rato. Luego da dos golpecitos en el cristal.\n\nSale una carta distinta.",
    "The box takes the cog, clicks once, and unfolds a drawer from somewhere no drawer should fit. Then a second. Then a third.\n\nIt climbs into your pack and settles in like it has always been there.\n\nLoyal Latchbox: +1 inventory slot": "La caja coge el engranaje, hace clic y despliega un cajón de donde no debería caber ninguno. Luego otro. Luego un tercero.\n\nSe mete en tu mochila y se acomoda como si siempre hubiera estado ahí.\n\nCaja Fiel: +1 espacio de inventario",
    "The box swallows the cog. It clicks. It coughs smoke.\n\nThen it plays three flat notes, spits a handful of valuables at your feet, and refuses to look at you.": "La caja se traga el engranaje. Hace clic. Tose humo.\n\nLuego toca tres notas desafinadas, escupe un puñado de objetos de valor a tus pies y se niega a mirarte.",
    "\"Free repair is still repair,\" the goblin says. \"Just shorter.\"": "«Una reparación gratis sigue siendo una reparación», dice el goblin. «Solo que más corta».",
    "He chews the card thoughtfully, then bolts half of it into the casing. \"Good enough for a machine with low standards.\"": "Mastica la carta pensativo y luego atornilla la mitad a la carcasa. «Basta para una máquina poco exigente».",
    "He counts the coins twice. Then he becomes suddenly, completely professional, which is somehow worse.": "Cuenta las monedas dos veces. Luego se vuelve de pronto completamente profesional, lo cual es peor por algún motivo.",
    "The ogre is at the same table. He has not put his coins back out.\n\nInstead he has unbuckled the stone guard from his forearm and laid it on the slab between you. It is scaled, heavy, and clearly not his originally.\n\nThe crowd is bigger this time, and much quieter.\n\n{crowd}": "El ogro está en la misma mesa. No ha vuelto a sacar las monedas.\n\nEn su lugar se ha quitado el protector de piedra del antebrazo y lo ha puesto en la losa, entre los dos. Tiene escamas, pesa y está claro que no era suyo.\n\nEsta vez hay más público y mucho menos ruido.\n\n{crowd}",
    "An ogre sits at a stone table with one elbow planted on it. Coins are stacked by his hand — more than a goblin toll, less than he seems to think.\n\nA stool waits on your side. It is too small.\n\nMonsters have gathered to watch: a few goblins, something with too many legs, and a skeleton that keeps losing its place in the crowd.\n\n{crowd}": "Un ogro está sentado a una mesa de piedra, con un codo plantado en ella. Junto a su mano hay monedas apiladas: más que un peaje goblin, menos de lo que él parece creer.\n\nEn tu lado hay un taburete. Es demasiado pequeño.\n\nSe han reunido monstruos para mirar: unos goblins, algo con demasiadas patas y un esqueleto que no deja de perder su sitio entre el público.\n\n{crowd}",
    "You leave the guard where it is.\n\nThe ogre says something in Ogrish that the crowd finds funnier than you do, and buckles it back onto his arm.": "Dejas el protector donde está.\n\nEl ogro dice algo en ogresco que al público le hace más gracia que a ti y se lo vuelve a abrochar en el brazo.",
    "He mutters something in Ogrish. The crowd loses interest in you immediately.\n\nThe stool stays empty.": "Murmura algo en ogresco. El público pierde el interés en ti al instante.\n\nEl taburete sigue vacío.",
    "(Drag a weapon onto a case.)": "(Arrastra un arma a una vitrina.)",
    "(You have no weapon to trade.)": "(No tienes armas para el trueque.)",
    "The corridor ends at a wall of glass cases. Most are broken and empty. {lit} are not.\n\nBRING IRON. LEAVE CHANGED — carved beneath them, and scratched under the empty cases in worse handwriting.\n\n{dragLine}": "El corredor termina en una pared de vitrinas de cristal. Casi todas están rotas y vacías. {lit} no lo están.\n\nTRAE HIERRO. SAL DISTINTO: está grabado debajo y arañado bajo las vitrinas vacías, con peor letra.\n\n{dragLine}",
    "You go along the wall, feeling through the broken cases.\n\nMost hold nothing but glass. One still has something wedged in the corner.": "Recorres la pared, tanteando entre las vitrinas rotas.\n\nEn casi todas solo hay cristal. En una aún queda algo encajado en la esquina.",
    "\n\nBehind you, {names} keep turning in their cases, waiting for iron that does not come.": "\n\nA tu espalda, {names} siguen girando en sus vitrinas, esperando un hierro que no llega.",
    "You leave the wall alone.": "Dejas la pared en paz.",
});
Object.assign(EVENT_NARRATIVE_TRANSLATIONS.fr, {
    "You push the gem past the teeth. It rolls up into an eye socket and fits exactly.\n\nRed light spreads through the cracks in the face. The head exhales one slow cloud of dust — and when it clears, a Fire Rune is resting on the stone tongue.": "Vous poussez la gemme entre les dents. Elle roule jusqu’à une orbite et s’y loge exactement.\n\nUne lumière rouge gagne les fissures du visage. La tête expire lentement un nuage de poussière. Quand il se dissipe, une rune de feu repose sur la langue de pierre.",
    "You push the gem past the teeth. It clicks into an eye socket.\n\nA thin bolt skips across the cracked forehead, and the teeth chatter once. The head exhales dust — and a Lightning Rune flickers between its teeth.": "Vous poussez la gemme entre les dents. Elle se loge dans une orbite avec un déclic.\n\nUn éclair fin parcourt le front fissuré et les dents claquent une fois. La tête expire de la poussière. Une Rune de foudre clignote entre ses dents.",
    "You push the gem past the teeth. It settles into an eye socket.\n\nGreen light seeps through the cracks, and the mouth curls — almost like remembering pain. The head exhales a bitter cloud. Behind it, a dark green rune rests on the stone tongue.": "Vous poussez la gemme entre les dents. Elle se cale dans une orbite.\n\nUne lumière verte filtre par les fissures et la bouche se tord, presque comme au souvenir d’une douleur. La tête expire un nuage âcre. Derrière, une rune vert sombre repose sur la langue de pierre.",
    "You set the Crystal Spiderling card down on the cracked floor of the drill room.\n\nThe spiderling climbs off the card, taps along the cracks and pulls a grain of crystal out of one.\n\nIt climbs back into the picture and keeps the grain.": "Vous posez la carte de la Petite araignée de cristal sur le sol fissuré de la salle d’entraînement.\n\nL’araignée sort de la carte, tapote les fissures et tire de l’une d’elles un grain de cristal.\n\nElle rentre dans l’image et garde le grain.",
    "You slide the card between the stone teeth.\n\nThe mouth closes. Stone grinds on stone, and for a few seconds the head chews.\n\nThen the jaw cracks open. A different card is lying on the tongue, damp with gray dust.": "Vous glissez la carte entre les dents de pierre.\n\nLa bouche se ferme. La pierre grince contre la pierre et, quelques secondes, la tête mâche.\n\nPuis la mâchoire s’ouvre en craquant. Une autre carte repose sur la langue, humide de poussière grise.",
    "You hold the card out to the vines.\n\nThey wrap it carefully — almost gently — and sink a few black thorns into its edge.\n\nWhen they let go, the card is not the same.": "Vous tendez la carte aux lianes.\n\nElles l’enveloppent avec soin, presque doucement, et plantent quelques épines noires dans son bord.\n\nQuand elles la lâchent, la carte n’est plus la même.",
    "A few of them stop chewing when they see what you are carrying. One goblin quietly moves round to your side of the table.": "Certains arrêtent de mâcher en voyant ce que vous portez. Un gobelin passe discrètement de votre côté de la table.",
    "Nobody moves. The thing with too many legs watches both of you and does not pick a side.": "Personne ne bouge. La chose qui a trop de pattes vous observe tous les deux sans choisir de camp.",
    "The whole room is already laughing. Someone starts collecting bets before you have sat down.": "Toute la salle rit déjà. Quelqu’un commence à prendre les paris avant même que vous soyez assis.",
    "He is stronger than you and both of you know it, so you do not try to out-pull him. You wait until he leans, and then you stop being where he is pushing.\n\nHis own weight takes his hand down onto the slab.\n\nThe room goes very quiet. The ogre looks at his hand for a while, then at you, and pushes the whole stack of coins across the table without a word.": "Il est plus fort que vous et vous le savez tous les deux. Vous n’essayez donc pas de gagner en force. Vous attendez qu’il se penche, puis cessez d’être là où il pousse.\n\nSon propre poids rabat sa main sur la dalle.\n\nLa salle devient très calme. L’ogre regarde sa main un moment, puis vous, et pousse toute la pile de pièces vers vous sans un mot.",
    "You get about two seconds of holding him.\n\nThen your knuckles find the stone.\n\nHe takes the coins. That is all he takes.": "Vous tenez à peu près deux secondes.\n\nPuis vos jointures trouvent la pierre.\n\nIl prend les pièces. C’est tout ce qu’il prend.",
    "He goes at it properly this time, and it takes everything you have.\n\nWhen his hand finally goes down the crowd does not cheer. They just look at the ogre.\n\nHe unhooks the stone guard and pushes it across to you, then sits back with his arms folded and watches you take it, {card} and all.": "Cette fois, il s’y met vraiment et vous donnez tout ce que vous avez.\n\nQuand sa main cède enfin, la foule n’applaudit pas. Elle regarde l’ogre.\n\nIl détache la protection de pierre et la pousse vers vous. Puis il se rassoit, les bras croisés, et vous regarde tout emporter, y compris votre carte : {card}.",
    "He looks at {card} for a long moment, decides it is worth his time, and plants his elbow.\n\nYou win by not fighting him where he is strongest.\n\nHe pushes his coins over, keeps looking at his own hand, and says something short in Ogrish. The crowd stops laughing. You get the distinct impression this is not finished.": "Il regarde la carte, {card}, un long moment, décide qu’elle vaut son temps et pose le coude.\n\nVous gagnez en évitant de l’affronter là où il est le plus fort.\n\nIl pousse ses pièces vers vous, regarde encore sa main et dit quelques mots en ogre. La foule cesse de rire. Vous avez la nette impression que ce n’est pas fini.",
    "He does not make the same mistake twice.\n\nYour hand is on the slab before you have finished bracing, and {card} goes into the pile beside his elbow.\n\nHe buckles the stone guard back onto his forearm and turns away from the table.": "Il ne fait pas deux fois la même erreur.\n\nVotre main est sur la dalle avant même que vous ayez fini de vous caler. Votre carte, {card}, rejoint la pile près de son coude.\n\nIl rattache la protection de pierre à son avant-bras et se détourne de la table.",
    "He takes {card} off the table before your hand has finished going down.\n\nThe crowd is delighted, briefly, and then bored.": "Il prend votre carte, {card}, sur la table avant que votre main ait fini de descendre.\n\nLa foule est ravie, un instant. Puis s’ennuie.",
    "You do not say anything. You draw the weapon and rest it against the doors, in the light, where all three of them can see it properly.\n\nThe one with the tally board stops writing. The one with the shield finds something interesting on the floor.\n\nNobody stops you lifting the lid of the strongbox at the foot of the door, and nobody looks at you either. The bar is already off by the time you straighten up.": "Vous ne dites rien. Vous sortez l’arme et l’appuyez contre les portes, dans la lumière, bien en vue de tous les trois.\n\nCelui qui tient le registre cesse d’écrire. Celui au bouclier trouve quelque chose d’intéressant par terre.\n\nPersonne ne vous empêche de soulever le couvercle du coffre au pied de la porte. Personne ne vous regarde non plus. Quand vous vous redressez, la barre est déjà retirée.",
    "You press the weapon flat against the glass.\n\nThe case opens from the inside. The {magic} settles against the metal and sinks in, and the glass closes over nothing.\n\nThe other cases go dark.\n\nWhat you are holding is called {weapon} now.": "Vous plaquez l’arme contre la vitre.\n\nLa vitrine s’ouvre de l’intérieur. La carte, {magic}, se pose contre le métal et s’y enfonce. La vitre se referme sur du vide.\n\nLes autres vitrines s’assombrissent.\n\nCe que vous tenez s’appelle maintenant {weapon}.",
    "You put your elbow through the nearest case.\n\nThe glass opens your arm. Whatever was inside is already gone.": "Vous passez le coude à travers la vitrine la plus proche.\n\nLe verre vous ouvre le bras. Ce qui était dedans a déjà disparu.",
    "You put your elbow through the case holding the {magic}.\n\nThe ward goes off late and shallow, opening a line across your forearm — but the card is in your fist and it stays there.\n\nThe remaining cases go dark before the glass finishes falling.": "Vous passez le coude à travers la vitrine qui contient la carte : {magic}.\n\nLa protection se déclenche tard et vous entaille à peine l’avant-bras. Mais la carte est dans votre poing et y reste.\n\nLes autres vitrines s’assombrissent avant que le verre ait fini de tomber.",
    "You hold the card out over the water. Your reflection lifts the wrong hand.\n\nThe card sinks without a sound. A different one comes up, cold and dripping tar.\n\nFor a second it feels like you made a deal with yourself.": "Vous tendez la carte au-dessus de l’eau. Votre reflet lève la mauvaise main.\n\nLa carte coule sans un bruit. Une autre remonte, froide et dégoulinante de goudron.\n\nUn instant, vous avez l’impression d’avoir passé un marché avec vous-même.",
    "You put the trinket on the tray. It snaps back into the booth.\n\nThe glass goes dark. Then a rainbow sheen spreads across it from the inside — thin and oily, like light on spilled ink.\n\nA card slides out. It is far too bright for the machine that made it.": "Vous posez la babiole sur le plateau. Il rentre d’un coup dans la cabine.\n\nLa vitre s’assombrit. Puis un reflet arc-en-ciel s’étale de l’intérieur, fin et huileux, comme de la lumière sur de l’encre renversée.\n\nUne carte sort. Elle est bien trop brillante pour la machine qui l’a faite.",
    "You put one of your cards on the tray. It snaps back before you can change your mind.\n\nBehind the glass, the wizard looks at the card for a long time. Then it taps the glass twice.\n\nA different card slides out.": "Vous posez une de vos cartes sur le plateau. Il rentre avant que vous puissiez changer d’avis.\n\nDerrière la vitre, le sorcier regarde longuement la carte. Puis il tape deux fois sur le verre.\n\nUne autre carte sort.",
    "The box takes the cog, clicks once, and unfolds a drawer from somewhere no drawer should fit. Then a second. Then a third.\n\nIt climbs into your pack and settles in like it has always been there.\n\nLoyal Latchbox: +1 inventory slot": "La boîte prend le rouage, clique une fois et déplie un tiroir là où aucun ne devrait tenir. Puis un deuxième. Puis un troisième.\n\nElle grimpe dans votre sac et s’installe comme si elle avait toujours été là.\n\nBoîte fidèle : +1 emplacement d’inventaire",
    "The box swallows the cog. It clicks. It coughs smoke.\n\nThen it plays three flat notes, spits a handful of valuables at your feet, and refuses to look at you.": "La boîte avale le rouage. Elle clique. Elle tousse de la fumée.\n\nPuis elle joue trois notes fausses, crache une poignée d’objets de valeur à vos pieds et refuse de vous regarder.",
    "\"Free repair is still repair,\" the goblin says. \"Just shorter.\"": "« Une réparation gratuite reste une réparation, dit le gobelin. Juste plus courte. »",
    "He chews the card thoughtfully, then bolts half of it into the casing. \"Good enough for a machine with low standards.\"": "Il mâche la carte d’un air pensif, puis en boulonne la moitié dans le boîtier. « Ça suffira pour une machine peu exigeante. »",
    "He counts the coins twice. Then he becomes suddenly, completely professional, which is somehow worse.": "Il compte les pièces deux fois. Puis il devient soudain parfaitement professionnel, ce qui est pire, on ne sait pourquoi.",
    "The ogre is at the same table. He has not put his coins back out.\n\nInstead he has unbuckled the stone guard from his forearm and laid it on the slab between you. It is scaled, heavy, and clearly not his originally.\n\nThe crowd is bigger this time, and much quieter.\n\n{crowd}": "L’ogre est à la même table. Il n’a pas ressorti ses pièces.\n\nÀ la place, il a détaché la protection de pierre de son avant-bras et l’a posée sur la dalle entre vous. Elle est couverte d’écailles, lourde, et n’était clairement pas à lui à l’origine.\n\nLa foule est plus nombreuse cette fois, et bien plus calme.\n\n{crowd}",
    "An ogre sits at a stone table with one elbow planted on it. Coins are stacked by his hand — more than a goblin toll, less than he seems to think.\n\nA stool waits on your side. It is too small.\n\nMonsters have gathered to watch: a few goblins, something with too many legs, and a skeleton that keeps losing its place in the crowd.\n\n{crowd}": "Un ogre est assis à une table de pierre, un coude posé dessus. Des pièces sont empilées près de sa main. Plus qu’un péage gobelin, moins qu’il ne semble le croire.\n\nUn tabouret vous attend de votre côté. Il est trop petit.\n\nDes monstres se sont rassemblés pour regarder : quelques gobelins, quelque chose avec trop de pattes et un squelette qui perd sans cesse sa place dans la foule.\n\n{crowd}",
    "You leave the guard where it is.\n\nThe ogre says something in Ogrish that the crowd finds funnier than you do, and buckles it back onto his arm.": "Vous laissez la protection en place.\n\nL’ogre dit quelque chose en ogre qui amuse la foule plus que vous, puis la rattache à son bras.",
    "He mutters something in Ogrish. The crowd loses interest in you immediately.\n\nThe stool stays empty.": "Il marmonne quelque chose en ogre. La foule se désintéresse aussitôt de vous.\n\nLe tabouret reste vide.",
    "(Drag a weapon onto a case.)": "(Glissez une arme sur une vitrine.)",
    "(You have no weapon to trade.)": "(Vous n’avez pas d’arme à échanger.)",
    "The corridor ends at a wall of glass cases. Most are broken and empty. {lit} are not.\n\nBRING IRON. LEAVE CHANGED — carved beneath them, and scratched under the empty cases in worse handwriting.\n\n{dragLine}": "Le couloir se termine devant un mur de vitrines. La plupart sont brisées et vides. {lit} ne le sont pas.\n\nAPPORTEZ DU FER. REPARTEZ CHANGÉ — gravé dessous et griffonné sous les vitrines vides, d’une écriture moins soignée.\n\n{dragLine}",
    "You go along the wall, feeling through the broken cases.\n\nMost hold nothing but glass. One still has something wedged in the corner.": "Vous longez le mur en fouillant à tâtons les vitrines brisées.\n\nLa plupart ne contiennent que du verre. Dans l’une, quelque chose est encore coincé dans un coin.",
    "\n\nBehind you, {names} keep turning in their cases, waiting for iron that does not come.": "\n\nDerrière vous, {names} tournent encore dans leurs vitrines, attendant du fer qui ne vient pas.",
    "You leave the wall alone.": "Vous laissez le mur tranquille.",
});
Object.assign(EVENT_NARRATIVE_TRANSLATIONS.ru, {
    "You push the gem past the teeth. It rolls up into an eye socket and fits exactly.\n\nRed light spreads through the cracks in the face. The head exhales one slow cloud of dust — and when it clears, a Fire Rune is resting on the stone tongue.": "Вы проталкиваете камень между зубами. Он закатывается в глазницу и точно встаёт на место.\n\nПо трещинам на лице разливается красный свет. Голова медленно выдыхает облако пыли. Когда оно рассеивается, на каменном языке лежит Руна огня.",
    "You push the gem past the teeth. It clicks into an eye socket.\n\nA thin bolt skips across the cracked forehead, and the teeth chatter once. The head exhales dust — and a Lightning Rune flickers between its teeth.": "Вы проталкиваете камень между зубами. Он со щелчком встаёт в глазницу.\n\nТонкая молния пробегает по треснувшему лбу. Зубы разок стучат. Голова выдыхает пыль. Между зубами мерцает Руна молнии.",
    "You push the gem past the teeth. It settles into an eye socket.\n\nGreen light seeps through the cracks, and the mouth curls — almost like remembering pain. The head exhales a bitter cloud. Behind it, a dark green rune rests on the stone tongue.": "Вы проталкиваете камень между зубами. Он ложится в глазницу.\n\nИз трещин сочится зелёный свет, рот кривится, словно вспомнив боль. Голова выдыхает горькое облако. За ним на каменном языке лежит тёмно-зелёная руна.",
    "You set the Crystal Spiderling card down on the cracked floor of the drill room.\n\nThe spiderling climbs off the card, taps along the cracks and pulls a grain of crystal out of one.\n\nIt climbs back into the picture and keeps the grain.": "Вы кладёте карту Хрустального паучка на потрескавшийся пол тренировочной комнаты.\n\nПаучок вылезает из карты, простукивает трещины и вытаскивает из одной кристальное зёрнышко.\n\nПотом возвращается в картинку. Зёрнышко оставляет себе.",
    "You slide the card between the stone teeth.\n\nThe mouth closes. Stone grinds on stone, and for a few seconds the head chews.\n\nThen the jaw cracks open. A different card is lying on the tongue, damp with gray dust.": "Вы просовываете карту между каменными зубами.\n\nРот закрывается. Камень скрежещет о камень. Несколько секунд голова жуёт.\n\nПотом челюсть с треском раскрывается. На языке лежит другая карта, влажная от серой пыли.",
    "You hold the card out to the vines.\n\nThey wrap it carefully — almost gently — and sink a few black thorns into its edge.\n\nWhen they let go, the card is not the same.": "Вы протягиваете карту лозам.\n\nОни осторожно, почти нежно обвивают её и вонзают в край несколько чёрных шипов.\n\nКогда они отпускают карту, она уже другая.",
    "A few of them stop chewing when they see what you are carrying. One goblin quietly moves round to your side of the table.": "Увидев, что у вас с собой, некоторые перестают жевать. Один гоблин тихонько переходит на вашу сторону стола.",
    "Nobody moves. The thing with too many legs watches both of you and does not pick a side.": "Никто не двигается. Существо с лишними ногами смотрит на вас обоих и не выбирает сторону.",
    "The whole room is already laughing. Someone starts collecting bets before you have sat down.": "Вся комната уже смеётся. Кто-то начинает собирать ставки, пока вы ещё не сели.",
    "He is stronger than you and both of you know it, so you do not try to out-pull him. You wait until he leans, and then you stop being where he is pushing.\n\nHis own weight takes his hand down onto the slab.\n\nThe room goes very quiet. The ogre looks at his hand for a while, then at you, and pushes the whole stack of coins across the table without a word.": "Он сильнее вас, и вы оба это знаете. Силой его не одолеть. Вы ждёте, пока он наклонится, и перестаёте быть там, куда он давит.\n\nПод собственным весом его рука ложится на плиту.\n\nВ комнате становится очень тихо. Огр некоторое время смотрит на свою руку, потом на вас. Молча пододвигает к вам всю стопку монет.",
    "You get about two seconds of holding him.\n\nThen your knuckles find the stone.\n\nHe takes the coins. That is all he takes.": "Вы держитесь примерно две секунды.\n\nПотом костяшки находят камень.\n\nОн забирает монеты. Только монеты.",
    "He goes at it properly this time, and it takes everything you have.\n\nWhen his hand finally goes down the crowd does not cheer. They just look at the ogre.\n\nHe unhooks the stone guard and pushes it across to you, then sits back with his arms folded and watches you take it, {card} and all.": "На этот раз он берётся всерьёз, и вам приходится выложиться полностью.\n\nКогда его рука наконец ложится на стол, толпа не ликует. Все просто смотрят на огра.\n\nОн отстёгивает каменный наруч и пододвигает к вам. Потом откидывается, скрестив руки, и смотрит, как вы забираете всё, включая свою карту: {card}.",
    "He looks at {card} for a long moment, decides it is worth his time, and plants his elbow.\n\nYou win by not fighting him where he is strongest.\n\nHe pushes his coins over, keeps looking at his own hand, and says something short in Ogrish. The crowd stops laughing. You get the distinct impression this is not finished.": "Он долго смотрит на карту — {card}, решает, что она стоит его времени, и ставит локоть на стол.\n\nВы побеждаете, не меряясь с ним силой там, где он сильнее.\n\nОн пододвигает вам монеты, всё смотрит на свою руку и коротко говорит что-то по-огрски. Толпа перестаёт смеяться. Вам становится ясно: это ещё не конец.",
    "He does not make the same mistake twice.\n\nYour hand is on the slab before you have finished bracing, and {card} goes into the pile beside his elbow.\n\nHe buckles the stone guard back onto his forearm and turns away from the table.": "Он не повторяет ошибок.\n\nВы ещё не успели упереться, а рука уже на плите. Ваша карта, {card}, отправляется в кучу у его локтя.\n\nОн застёгивает каменный наруч на предплечье и отворачивается от стола.",
    "He takes {card} off the table before your hand has finished going down.\n\nThe crowd is delighted, briefly, and then bored.": "Он забирает вашу карту, {card}, со стола раньше, чем ваша рука успевает опуститься.\n\nТолпа в восторге. Недолго. Потом ей скучно.",
    "You do not say anything. You draw the weapon and rest it against the doors, in the light, where all three of them can see it properly.\n\nThe one with the tally board stops writing. The one with the shield finds something interesting on the floor.\n\nNobody stops you lifting the lid of the strongbox at the foot of the door, and nobody looks at you either. The bar is already off by the time you straighten up.": "Вы ничего не говорите. Достаёте оружие и прислоняете к дверям, на свету, чтобы все трое хорошенько разглядели.\n\nТот, что с дощечкой для подсчётов, перестаёт писать. Тот, что со щитом, находит на полу что-то интересное.\n\nНикто не мешает вам открыть сундук у двери. На вас тоже никто не смотрит. Когда вы выпрямляетесь, засов уже снят.",
    "You press the weapon flat against the glass.\n\nThe case opens from the inside. The {magic} settles against the metal and sinks in, and the glass closes over nothing.\n\nThe other cases go dark.\n\nWhat you are holding is called {weapon} now.": "Вы прижимаете оружие плашмя к стеклу.\n\nВитрина открывается изнутри. Карта, {magic}, ложится на металл и уходит в него. Стекло закрывается над пустотой.\n\nОстальные витрины гаснут.\n\nТеперь то, что вы держите, называется {weapon}.",
    "You put your elbow through the nearest case.\n\nThe glass opens your arm. Whatever was inside is already gone.": "Вы пробиваете локтем ближайшую витрину.\n\nСтекло распарывает руку. Что бы ни было внутри, оно уже исчезло.",
    "You put your elbow through the case holding the {magic}.\n\nThe ward goes off late and shallow, opening a line across your forearm — but the card is in your fist and it stays there.\n\nThe remaining cases go dark before the glass finishes falling.": "Вы пробиваете локтем витрину с картой: {magic}.\n\nЗащита срабатывает поздно и лишь слегка рассекает предплечье. Но карта уже в вашем кулаке и там остаётся.\n\nОстальные витрины гаснут, прежде чем стекло успевает упасть.",
    "You hold the card out over the water. Your reflection lifts the wrong hand.\n\nThe card sinks without a sound. A different one comes up, cold and dripping tar.\n\nFor a second it feels like you made a deal with yourself.": "Вы протягиваете карту над водой. Отражение поднимает не ту руку.\n\nКарта беззвучно тонет. Другая всплывает, холодная, с неё капает дёготь.\n\nНа секунду кажется, что вы заключили сделку с собой.",
    "You put the trinket on the tray. It snaps back into the booth.\n\nThe glass goes dark. Then a rainbow sheen spreads across it from the inside — thin and oily, like light on spilled ink.\n\nA card slides out. It is far too bright for the machine that made it.": "Вы кладёте безделушку на поднос. Он резко уходит внутрь будки.\n\nСтекло темнеет. Потом изнутри по нему растекается тонкий маслянистый радужный блеск, как свет по пролитым чернилам.\n\nВыдвигается карта. Слишком яркая для машины, которая её сделала.",
    "You put one of your cards on the tray. It snaps back before you can change your mind.\n\nBehind the glass, the wizard looks at the card for a long time. Then it taps the glass twice.\n\nA different card slides out.": "Вы кладёте одну из своих карт на поднос. Он уходит внутрь прежде, чем вы успеваете передумать.\n\nЗа стеклом волшебник долго смотрит на карту. Потом дважды стучит по стеклу.\n\nВыдвигается другая карта.",
    "The box takes the cog, clicks once, and unfolds a drawer from somewhere no drawer should fit. Then a second. Then a third.\n\nIt climbs into your pack and settles in like it has always been there.\n\nLoyal Latchbox: +1 inventory slot": "Шкатулка берёт шестерёнку, разок щёлкает и выдвигает ящик оттуда, где никакой ящик не должен помещаться. Потом второй. Потом третий.\n\nОна залезает в ваш рюкзак и устраивается так, будто всегда там жила.\n\nВерная шкатулка: +1 ячейка инвентаря",
    "The box swallows the cog. It clicks. It coughs smoke.\n\nThen it plays three flat notes, spits a handful of valuables at your feet, and refuses to look at you.": "Шкатулка глотает шестерёнку. Щёлкает. Кашляет дымом.\n\nПотом фальшиво играет три ноты, выплёвывает горсть ценностей вам под ноги и отказывается на вас смотреть.",
    "\"Free repair is still repair,\" the goblin says. \"Just shorter.\"": "«Бесплатный ремонт тоже ремонт, — говорит гоблин. — Просто короче».",
    "He chews the card thoughtfully, then bolts half of it into the casing. \"Good enough for a machine with low standards.\"": "Он задумчиво жуёт карту, потом прикручивает половину к корпусу. «Для непритязательной машины сойдёт».",
    "He counts the coins twice. Then he becomes suddenly, completely professional, which is somehow worse.": "Он дважды пересчитывает монеты. Потом вдруг становится безупречным профессионалом, что почему-то ещё хуже.",
    "The ogre is at the same table. He has not put his coins back out.\n\nInstead he has unbuckled the stone guard from his forearm and laid it on the slab between you. It is scaled, heavy, and clearly not his originally.\n\nThe crowd is bigger this time, and much quieter.\n\n{crowd}": "Огр за тем же столом. Монеты он обратно не выложил.\n\nВместо них он снял с предплечья каменный наруч и положил на плиту между вами. Чешуйчатый, тяжёлый и явно изначально не его.\n\nТолпа на этот раз больше и гораздо тише.\n\n{crowd}",
    "An ogre sits at a stone table with one elbow planted on it. Coins are stacked by his hand — more than a goblin toll, less than he seems to think.\n\nA stool waits on your side. It is too small.\n\nMonsters have gathered to watch: a few goblins, something with too many legs, and a skeleton that keeps losing its place in the crowd.\n\n{crowd}": "За каменным столом сидит огр, уперев в него локоть. У руки сложены монеты. Больше, чем берут гоблины за проход. Меньше, чем ему, похоже, кажется.\n\nС вашей стороны ждёт табуретка. Слишком маленькая.\n\nПосмотреть собрались чудовища: несколько гоблинов, что-то с лишними ногами и скелет, который всё теряет своё место в толпе.\n\n{crowd}",
    "You leave the guard where it is.\n\nThe ogre says something in Ogrish that the crowd finds funnier than you do, and buckles it back onto his arm.": "Вы оставляете наруч на месте.\n\nОгр говорит что-то по-огрски. Толпе смешнее, чем вам. Он снова застёгивает наруч на руке.",
    "He mutters something in Ogrish. The crowd loses interest in you immediately.\n\nThe stool stays empty.": "Он бормочет что-то по-огрски. Толпа тут же теряет к вам интерес.\n\nТабуретка остаётся пустой.",
    "(Drag a weapon onto a case.)": "(Перетащите оружие на витрину.)",
    "(You have no weapon to trade.)": "(У вас нет оружия для обмена.)",
    "The corridor ends at a wall of glass cases. Most are broken and empty. {lit} are not.\n\nBRING IRON. LEAVE CHANGED — carved beneath them, and scratched under the empty cases in worse handwriting.\n\n{dragLine}": "Коридор кончается стеной стеклянных витрин. Большинство разбиты и пусты. {lit} — нет.\n\nПРИНЕСИ ЖЕЛЕЗО. УЙДИ ДРУГИМ — высечено под ними и нацарапано под пустыми витринами почерком похуже.\n\n{dragLine}",
    "You go along the wall, feeling through the broken cases.\n\nMost hold nothing but glass. One still has something wedged in the corner.": "Вы идёте вдоль стены, ощупывая разбитые витрины.\n\nВ большинстве только стекло. В одной ещё что-то застряло в углу.",
    "\n\nBehind you, {names} keep turning in their cases, waiting for iron that does not come.": "\n\nПозади {names} всё вращаются в витринах, ожидая железа, которого так и нет.",
    "You leave the wall alone.": "Вы оставляете стену в покое.",
});
